gametitle=Drakengard (SLUS-20732) CRC 9679D44C

[Core: input hooks, button mapping and pad fixes]
author=Shade
description=Input hooks that many other sections need, the default button mapping and the pad table cleanup after aerial stages.
// 3 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Input core: player input hook and levels marker (needed by the Aerial controls, block special and lock-on sections) =====
// Split out of the old "Controls remap" section on 2026-10-27. The pad remap itself is no longer done here: the old button-table cave T (00321E40, hook 001316E4) was overwritten by the Aerial section (which moved the pad-update hook to its cave T2 at 00321A20 and does the table writes) and by later caves that reuse 00321E40..00321F88, so it was dropped. The old Cross -> sideways dodge part of RS was already skipped by the Aerial section (00321A1C).
// What is left: the player input cave RS is entered from the jr ra at 0013E528 (j 00321A10) every frame in levels. It sets 00321E30 = 30 (the "levels" marker the Aerial cave T2 reads to apply its button table), then branches to 00321AD0 (block special) which ends in j 00321CA8 (R3 lock-on toggle), which ends in jr ra. Without those sections the stubs here jump straight on: 00321AD0 = j 00321CA8 and 00321CA8 = jr ra. The Aerial section jumps into 00321A10, so it needs this section (without it the level hangs on a black loading screen).
patch=1,EE,00321A10,word,3C180032
patch=1,EE,00321A14,word,3419001E
patch=1,EE,00321A18,word,AF191E30
// ===== Ground: pad table cleaned after an aerial stage (L3 sprint works after the seamless transition) =====
// Found with states taken after an aerial stage flowed straight into a ground level (L3 opened the weapon select instead of sprinting) and after a fresh ground load (works): the game builds the pad action table at 005747A0 when a level loads, and the aerial cave AER (00340904) edits it while flying: it ORs 0x0002 (L3 = glide) into the entries 005747AA / 005747AE and 0x0004 (R3 = switch target) into 005747B0. A seamless transition does not rebuild the table, so on the ground 005747AA stayed 0x1002 (Triangle + L3 = weapon select) and 005747AE 0x0002, 005747B0 0x0024, against 0x1000 / 0x0000 / 0x0020 after a fresh load; L3 therefore triggered the weapon select and the L3 sprint of the constant run speed section never saw it as free. The ground branch of the pad update cave (T2, only reached when the stage is not aerial and the remap counter is running) ends its table edits with sh t5,0x47B0(t2) at 00321A74. That word becomes j CLRPAD (005B6D00); the lui in its delay slot still runs. CLRPAD redoes the sh and then clears the L3 / R3 bits (andi 0xFFF9) in 005747AA, 005747AE and 005747B0 every frame and returns to 00321A7C. These bits are zero in a fresh ground table anyway, so nothing changes there. Aerial stages never reach this code (T2 leaves at 00321A38).
patch=1,EE,005B6D00,word,A54D47B0
patch=1,EE,005B6D04,word,954B47AA
patch=1,EE,005B6D08,word,316BFFF9
patch=1,EE,005B6D0C,word,A54B47AA
patch=1,EE,005B6D10,word,954B47AE
patch=1,EE,005B6D14,word,316BFFF9
patch=1,EE,005B6D18,word,A54B47AE
patch=1,EE,005B6D1C,word,954B47B0
patch=1,EE,005B6D20,word,316BFFF9
patch=1,EE,005B6D24,word,A54B47B0
patch=1,EE,005B6D28,word,080C869F
patch=1,EE,005B6D2C,word,00000000
// ===== Controls: your in-game button mapping is the default for a new save / Default button =====
// The game's default button table is 12 + 20 bytes at 00555F28 in the program data (copied to the live table 005747A0 by the reset code at 00131D00; halfword masks at +0x00..+0x13 = action -> button bits, bytes at +0x14..+0x1F = button index per action). The values of your current table (from a save state) replace the default: the three action masks AA / AC / AE (default 0200 0100 0200, yours 1000 0000 0000) and the 12 button index bytes (default 02 03 0B 08 08 09 0E 0A 0A 0D 0C 00, yours 02 03 0F 0D 0D 0C 0E 0E 0A 09 0B 00). The masks of A4 / A6 / A8 / B0 are not copied: the D-pad actions section rewrites them every frame in levels, so their saved values cannot be read from a state.
patch=1,EE,00555F30,word,10000002
patch=1,EE,00555F34,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00555F3C,word,0D0F0302
patch=1,EE,00555F40,word,0E0E0C0D
patch=1,EE,00555F44,word,000B090A

[Caim: movement, sprint, dodges and air dash]
author=Shade
description=Run speed, L3 sprint and super sprint, dodges and rolls, turning, direction changes, the air dash and the lean into curves.
// 19 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Caim: constant run speed + L3 sprint (press to start) =====
// Caim moves at a constant run speed. One press of L3 latches a sprint: speed glides to 1.5x, the wind burst plays once at the start, and the sprint attack unlocks. The sprint survives a jump and ends when you stop moving or use the sprint attack. Locomotion animation requests use the engine's default (short) cross-fade. Without L3 the burst never triggers.
// History notes (see also the project memory): an experiment that forced the animation engine's fade weight
// to full (hook at 0012DE38) broke run animations after any action and was removed. 00149B90 is controller
// RUMBLE (id -> strength table), not a visual effect; the rumble id 0xA fires at 0017087C when timer >= 0x400
// and 0x110(actor) bit 0x80.
//
// L3 = bit 1 of the pad data byte at 0056CD82 (player-1 pad object at 0056CD80; active low: 0 = pressed).
//
// State (both are unreachable padding nops, zero at boot):
//   002F345C  latch L (0/1)       002F340C  m = speed multiplier (float; 1.0 normal, 1.5 sprint)
// The walk timer (actor+0x6A0) is zeroed by the game when the player stops moving, at jump takeoff
// (00175498) and when a sprint attack is used (00173D24); the game raises it each frame and caps it at 0x4000.
// timer >= 0x4000 unlocks the sprint attack. The wind burst VISUAL plays when the game's own step takes the
// timer across 0x4000 (found by holding the timer at 0x3FFF: the wind then replayed every frame).
//
// Per frame (rewrites the old walk->run blend at 001701A8..001701F8, now dead code):
//   small = (timer < 0x200)               true during the first ~0.1s after the timer was zeroed
//   if (small) L = 0                      the player stopped / attacked (a jump with L keeps timer 0x4000)
//   if (L3 pressed) L = 1
//   below = (timer < 0x4000)              (the timer as the game left it this frame)
//   t = min(timer, 0x3FF)
//   if (L) timer = below ? 0x3FFF : 0x4000   0x3FFF on the first sprint frame so the game's step crosses 0x4000
//                                          ONCE (wind plays once), then the cap holds it at 0x4000
//   else   timer = t                      no automatic burst / effect while moving normally
//   if (small) m = 1.0
//   m += ((L ? 1.5 : 1.0) - m) * 0.22     (0.22 per frame; 3C063E61 at 0031B664)
//   f20 = runSpeed(f26) * m
//   Registers used: v0, v1, a0, a1, a2, a3, t0, t1, f0-f2 (dead at this point in the function).
//   NOTE: the hook's delay slot (lh v1,0x1a(s4)) clobbers v1, so nothing is carried in v1 across the hook.
//   Tuning: sprint level = 1.5 (sll by 22 adds 0.5 to the 1.0 base: 3C023F80 at 001701F8);
//           glide rate = lui at 0031B664 (3C063E61 ~0.22/frame; 3C063E10 ~0.14 slower).
patch=1,EE,001701A8,word,3C030057
patch=1,EE,001701AC,word,9063CD82
patch=1,EE,001701B0,word,3C04002F
patch=1,EE,001701B4,word,8C85345C
