// 2026-11-15 removed unused code: 32695C..326978 (nothing jumped, branched or loaded into it; the words were all zero in the original; no fall-through in or out).
// Jump takeoff (0017549x): the game does "if (a jump started /*s3*/) timer = 0" via a branch-likely delay slot.
// Replaced so that a latched sprint survives the jump: timer = L ? 0x4000 : 0 (L = latch word 002F345C).
//   00175494  was: bnel s3,zero,0017549C    now: j 003086A4
//   00175498  was: sw zero,0x6A0(s1)        now: lui v1,0x2F   (delay slot; v1 is dead here)
// Cave 3 at 003086A4 (six nops that precede an error-hang loop; only reached after a fatal error):
//   beq s3,zero,End ; lw v0,0x345C(v1) [delay] ; sll v0,v0,14 ; sw v0,0x6A0(s1) ; End: j 0017549C ; nop
patch=1,EE,00175494,word,0816CC00
patch=1,EE,00175498,word,3C03002F
// 2026-11-15 removed unused code: 3086A4..3086B8 (nothing jumped, branched or loaded into it; the words were all zero in the original; no fall-through in or out).
// Replaces cave 3 above (the hook 00175494 now jumps here, JMPC): the same work when a jump started (s3 != 0), and it also zeroes the super sprint count word 005B1F00 (SSC section), so the sprint after a jump starts at normal sprint speed and the 5 second count starts again.
//   005B3000  beq s3,zero,End(005B3018) ; lw v0,0x345C(v1) [delay] ; sll v0,v0,14 ; sw v0,0x6A0(s1)
//   005B3010  lui v0,0x5B ; sw zero,0x1F00(v0) ; j 0017549C ; nop
patch=1,EE,005B3000,word,12600005
