// Locomotion animation request (walk function, 001706D8..00170748), found by watching writes to actor+0x172:
//   FUN_0016EEF8 picks the animation from |movement vector| / walkSpeed (idle 0x21, walk 0x2A, jog 0x2B, run 0x2C)
//   and the request written to actor+0x170.. is: 0x170 = type (1/3), 0x172 = animation id,
//   0x174 = playback RATE (forcing it to 1 froze all animations),
//   0x176 = blend argument for type-1 requests (confirmed: zeroing it ends landing / pose holds sooner;
//           zero means "use the animation object's default blend").
//   Store 0 into 0x176 for the type-1 request (0017071C) and the type-3 request (00170740).
//   Originals: 0017071C = sh v1,0x176(s2), 00170740 = sh a0,0x176(s2).
// ===== Caim: faster run start and stop transitions (blend 4x faster) =====
// Locomotion animation requests (walk function 001706D8..): the animation parameter table (003BADB0, 16-byte entries: [0] id, [2] rate, [4] blend) gives the blend (cross-fade) of each locomotion animation (idle entry 0x21 = 0x400, walk 0x2A / jog 0x2B = 0x400, run 0x2C = 0x4000). The Caim sections stored 0 there (default blend). The type-1 and type-3 request stores (0017071C, 00170740) now jump to BL1 / BL2 (0033F1DC / 0033F1EC) which store the table blend divided by 4 (srl 2), so the transition into running and the transition to stopping are four times faster than vanilla.
patch=1,EE,0033F1DC,word,00031882
patch=1,EE,0033F1E0,word,A6430176
patch=1,EE,0033F1E4,word,0805C1C9
patch=1,EE,0033F1E8,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,0033F1EC,word,00042082
patch=1,EE,0033F1F0,word,A6440176
patch=1,EE,0033F1F4,word,0805C1D2
patch=1,EE,0033F1F8,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,0017071C,word,080CFC77
patch=1,EE,00170740,word,080CFC7B
// Run animation (table entry 0x2C, 003BB070: id 0xA5) blend 0x4000 -> 0x0400 so it takes over from the start-up animation sooner (after the /4 above its blend is 0x100, the same as the idle one).
patch=1,EE,003BB074,short,0400
// Idle animation (table entry 0x21, 003BAFC0: id 0x37) blend 0x400 -> 0x800 so after the /4 above the transition to stopping is 2x faster than vanilla (0x200) instead of 4x.
patch=1,EE,003BAFC4,short,0800
// 2026-10-28: the same two blends for the second animation table (003BB310, used by the other weapon class; rows 0x2C / 0x21 mirror the sword table), so those weapons get the same quick run start and stop.
patch=1,EE,003BB5D4,short,0400
patch=1,EE,003BB524,short,0800
// ===== Caim: dodge animations 2x while sprinting, 1.5x otherwise =====
// Caim dodge (roll, mode 3, FUN_00173E38): the animation request 00173EAC..EB8 picks row 0x4F (79) or 0x4E (78) of the animation parameter table (003BADB0, 16-byte rows, halfword 1 = playback rate, 0x1000 = 1.0; rows 78 / 79 = 003BB290 / 003BB2A0, ids 0xAE / 0xAF, vanilla rate 0x1000). The mode switch to the roll (FUN_001736C0, 001738F0 / 001738F4 become j ROLLC / nop, ROLLC at 0013E208 in the dead copy of the old double jump cave does the two stores itself) sets both rates just before the roll requests its animation: 0x1800 (1.5x), or 0x2000 (2x) when the sprint latch (word 002F345C) is on. DRON (00342CF8) = 1 switches that on. The same ROLLC also serves the sprint-resume-after-roll section.
patch=1,EE,00342CF8,word,00000001
// 2026-10-28: the two rate stores go through the game's current animation table pointer (word 0056A788 = gp-0x3768, the table FUN_0017E464 reads: 003BADB0 for swords, 003BB310 for the other weapon class) instead of the fixed sword rows, so every weapon gets the faster dodge: lw t3,-0x3768(gp) ; sh t2,0x4E2(t3) ; sh t2,0x4F2(t3).
// ===== Ground: free direction change in the air =====
// Jump phases FUN_001756B0 (takeoff) and FUN_00175BAC (flight) add the takeoff momentum [Caim+0x300] (x), [+0x308] (z) every frame and bend it / turn Caim a little with the stick (FUN_00147EB4, stick shorts +0x67C x, +0x67E y). The six lh that feed the stick into them (001757C0/C8, 00175938/44, 00175D0C/14) are replaced by daddu zero, so the game steers nothing itself (the lh at 001751EC that picks the side jump slash stays). Cave AIRC (part A 00341C94, momentum part M 003419B0, facing part B 0033ED40, constants pi / minimum speed at 0033EDA0 / 0033EDA4; entered from the third T2 placeholder Lph3, first nop turned into j AIRC, returns to Lph3+8; ground Caim only, t3 and t6 from T2) runs every frame while Caim is in the jump mode ([+0x2DC] == 5) in the phases [+0x2EC] 1..2 (takeoff, flight) and 3..5 (landing) of a jump type [+0x660] below 3 (the sprint jump attack / jump heavy attack lands like vanilla and stops) and the stick (shorts, already in Caim's frame) is outside the dead zone (squared radius about 155000, constant 0x4818 in the lui): D = x * right (+0x590, +0x598) - y * forward (+0x5B0, +0x5B8) (measured on the ground run) is the wanted direction. The momentum gets that direction with the ground speed Caim had before the jump (AIRGS 0033EDA8, recorded every frame of the ground run, mode [+0x2DC] == 2, by part R at 00342B48 from the position change +0x80/+0x88 minus +0x220/+0x228; sprint speed included), exactly (the air speed is capped at the takeoff speed, also a slow walk or standing, where there is no air movement; the word AIRSM 0033EDA4 is no longer used), and Caim is turned to D at once the way the lock-on routine FACE does it (yaw-delta accumulator +0x204 = wrapped difference to the yaw +0x44, flags +0x210 bit 1, +0x584 = yaw, +0x570 bit 0). The accumulator is cleared and refilled during the actor update, so a write from the pad update is lost: part B only stores the wanted yaw (AIRYAW 0033ED9C) and a flag (AIRFLG 0033ED98); the write itself is made inside the jump state by the hook at 00175470 (jal FUN_001754C0 becomes jal AIRH1 at 0033ED58, which ends in j 001754C0 and continues in AIRH2 at 00341A18). It needs the aerial section (routine ATAN at 00342E50) and is skipped without it.
// Own copy of the aerial atan2 helper ATAN (005B8000, same words as in the aerial section) so this section also works without the aerial section.
