// ===== Ground: sprint resumes after a sprint roll when the stick points forward (needs the constant run speed / L3 sprint section) =====
// 2026-10-30: the hook at 001701BC now goes to AUTOC2 (005BE280) instead of AUTOC. AUTOC2 first checks PEND (word 005BE1F8), which the Auto-attack cave AUTO sets to 0xFF while L3 is held during a ground combo (Caim state 2 / sub 4): in the first walk frames after the combo (20 frame window) a stick pushed to the edge (0xE00 of 0x1000 or more, any direction, Caim shorts +0x67C / +0x67E) presses L3 for the walk code, so Caim sprints at once. Without PEND the old AUTOC logic follows (flag 0033EDFC + stick forward). Needs the Auto-attack section for the buffering.
// The sprint of the constant-run-speed section is a latch (word 002F345C) that its hook in the walk function (001701A8..) clears whenever the walk timer [Caim+0x6A0] is below 0x200; the roll start (FUN_001736C0, 001738F0) zeroes the timer, so the first walk frame after a roll cleared the sprint. Cave ROLLC (00321FA0; 001738F0 / 001738F4 become j ROLLC / nop, ROLLC does the two stores itself) copies the latch into the flag word 0033EDFC when the new mode is the roll (3). Cave AUTOC (00321F70; 001701BC andi v1,v1,2 becomes j AUTOC, the sltiu in its delay slot stays) reads and clears the flag in the first walk frame after the roll: if it was set and the stick (short +0x67E in Caim's frame, forward = negative, below -0x800) points forward, v1 (the L3 bit of the pad, 0 = pressed) is set to 0, so the hook sees an L3 press: latch on, sprint speed, wind burst from the walk timer step as with a real press. Without a forward stick nothing is resumed (the sprint ends as before).
patch=1,EE,00321F70,word,30630002
patch=1,EE,00321F74,word,3C060034
