// ===== Caim: super sprint after 5 seconds of sprinting (needs the constant run speed / L3 sprint section) =====
// The sprint of the constant-run-speed section multiplies the run speed by m, gliding (0.22 per frame) to 1.0 normally and to 1.5 while the sprint latch (word 002F345C) is on: cave 1 at 0031B650 computes the target as 1.0f + (latch << 22) (0031B658 addu v0,v0,a3). That addu becomes j SSC (005B1000, always-zero bss; the mtc1 behind it runs in the delay slot with the old v0 and is redone there). SSC counts the walk frames while the latch is on (word 005B1F00, cleared when it is off, so it ends like a normal sprint: stop, sprint attack, a roll without a forward stick...; the roll start cave ROLLC also clears it, so a sprint that resumes after a roll is a regular sprint and the 5 seconds start again). Rates (current: sprint start 1.37, end of the 5 second ramp 1.70, super sprint 1.75; set 2026-10-23): SPB (word 005B1F0C) = the sprint multiplier, 1.37; during the first 300 frames (5 seconds at 60 fps; only walk frames count, so a jump pauses the count) the target ramps linearly from SPB to SRE (005B1F20, 1.6; 300.0 is the word at 005B1F08); from 300 frames the super sprint runs at SUP (005B1F04, 1.7): the target jumps to it and in that frame the walk timer [Caim+0x6A0] is set to 0x3000 (below 0x4000), so the sprint hook sends it through the 0x3FFF step again and the wind burst plays again. In addition the first sprint frame (count 1) and the super sprint start (count 300) always restart the burst slot ([Caim+0x560] = 0xEE, handle [+0x564] = 0), so the burst also plays when an earlier burst (the one after a combo) is still running in the slot.
patch=1,EE,005B1F0C,word,3FAF5C29
