// ===== Ground: wind burst after a combo ends when moving forward (needs the super sprint section) =====
// The player has an own wind burst effect slot: [Caim+0x560] = effect id 0xEE (the id of the L3 sprint burst), [+0x564] = its handle; the per-frame updater at 00178D0C creates / updates the effect from them. The sprint speed cave SSC (005B1000, hooked in the walk function; it belongs to the super sprint section, which has to be ticked too) now starts with a check: [Caim+0x6CC] holds the id of the last attack clip and is not cleared when the attack state ends, so it is non-zero in the first walk frame after an attack (the walk function does not run during the attack). With CBON (word 005B1F40, set to 1 by this section) the check clears 6CC and, if the stick is held in any direction in that frame (shorts +0x67C x / +0x67E y, |x| or |y| at least 0x400), starts the burst slot (0xEE, handle 0). With the stick at rest in that first frame nothing is played. The same burst plays after the R1 air attack: the cave DJ2B (slash double jump section) sets LANDF (word 005B1F4C) in every frame of the jump state with [+0x2EC] >= 3 (the landing phases, which only the R1 / sprint attack have), and the check treats LANDF like the 6CC value, so in the first walk frame after the landing the burst starts when the stick is held (needs the slash double jump section too).
patch=1,EE,005B1F40,word,00000001
// Combo started and ended standing still: the attack start end (00173D24, now j CHGC2 at 005B2680, which also does what CHGC does) stores 1 in 0033EDF0 when the stick (shorts +0x67C / +0x67E) is within 0x400 of the centre, else 0; the takeoff reset of the slash jump section clears it (00342C2C), so an air landing does not use an old value. In the super sprint cave the no-stick branch of the post-attack check (005B10AC) now goes to cave STAND (005B2600): with that flag set the wind burst plays as well, otherwise nothing as before.
patch=1,EE,005B2680,word,AE0006A0
