patch=0,EE,0033EDF0,word,00000000
// The walk function (where the post-attack check of the super sprint cave lives) does not run while Caim stands still, so the standing combo end was never seen (state: [+0x6CC] still set in the idle state). The per-frame call of the ground handler FUN_0016FB98 in the mode machine (001737C0, jal) now goes to cave STANDB (005B2700): if [+0x6CC] (last attack clip) is set (the standing flag and stick tests are now skipped: every combo that ends in the ground state, standing or moving, gets the burst) it creates the wind burst effect 0xEE directly (FUN_0019FCAC with the matrix at +0x50, raised by 12 as in the block charge test; ra, a0-a2 are saved in 005B2F90..9C), clears 6CC and the flag; then it jumps on to FUN_0016FB98 with the registers untouched (ra still points behind the original jal).
// Attached burst: after the effect is created (jal 0019FCAC returns the handle in v0) the handle goes to [Caim+0x564] and the id 0xEE to [Caim+0x560], so the per-frame updater at 00178D0C keeps moving the burst with Caim like the sprint burst.
patch=1,EE,005B2700,word,8E0806CC
