// ===== Ground: movement speed x2 while blocking =====
// Block action held (bit 0x80 of [Caim+0x66C], states with L2 held show 0x180): the mode 2 handler FUN_0016FB98 takes its block branch at 001700A0 (beq s7,zero,001701A8, s7 = block held) and walks with the speed f21 = f23 * 0.5 (001700A8 lui at,0x3F00 / mtc1 at,f1 / 001700B4 mul.S f21,f23,f1; f23 = the normal step speed, which the non-block walk of the same function uses as it is). The constant 0.5 becomes 0.75 (lui at,0x3F40), so the walking speed while blocking is 1.5 times as high (1.0 in the first try = 2x, exactly the speed of walking without the block; 0x3F80). It goes to FUN_00147DB8 / FUN_0014773C as the speed limit and step, so the animation request and the pose stay normal. (Earlier tries - doubling f22, adding the position step again - did nothing / broke the block animation.)
patch=1,EE,001700A8,word,3C013F40
// ===== Ground: wind burst when moving after a block is let go (needs the super sprint section and the combo burst section) =====
// While the block action is held, Caim walks in the block branch of the mode 2 handler FUN_0016FB98 (001700A8..), not in the walk function. 001700B0 (mtc1 zero,f0; the mul.S f21,f23,f1 behind it stays in the delay slot) becomes j BLKF (005B2000): the mtc1 is redone and the word BLKFL (005B1F54) is set to 30 in every block frame. The sprint speed cave SSC (005B1000, hooked in the walk function; needs the super sprint section, and CBON of the combo burst section) counts BLKFL down in every walk frame after the block is let go and, in the first of them (within 30 frames = half a second) in which the stick is held in any direction (|x| or |y| of the shorts +0x67C / +0x67E at least 0x400), starts the player wind burst slot ([Caim+0x560] = 0xEE, handle [+0x564] = 0) and clears BLKFL.
patch=1,EE,005B2000,word,44800000
