patch=0,EE,005B1F54,word,00000000
// ===== Ground: turn around when the stick is pulled straight back =====
// With the stick exactly opposite to the way Caim faces the turn step of the walk (FUN_00147560 steers by the sideways offset of the target, which is about 0 straight behind) is almost 0, so Caim walked backwards / stood and did not turn. Cave BACKT (005B2800, entered by replacing the daddu s2,a0,zero at 0016FBA0 in the prologue of the ground handler FUN_0016FB98, whose next word, the sd s4, runs in the delay slot; BACKT redoes the daddu and jumps to 0016FBA8): when the stick (shorts +0x67C x / +0x67E y at a1+0x18 / +0x1A, y positive = backward) is at least 0x800 backward and its sideways part is within 0x700, the sideways part is set to +-0x700 (the side of its sign, right when 0) so the turn starts at once; once Caim has turned the real sideways part is larger and nothing is changed. Not while the block action is held (bit 0x80 of [a1+8]).
// 2026-11-15 removed unused code: 5B2800..5B2850 (nothing jumped, branched or loaded into it; the words were all zero in the original; no fall-through in or out).
// ===== Ground: constant movement speed while turning (the run / walk animation stays too) =====
// The free walk branch of the ground handler FUN_0016FB98 chases a target frame (+0x570) with FUN_00147560; its displacement of the frame (vector at sp+0x20) gets shorter when Caim turns hard, and the animation class FUN_0016EEF8 picks (0x2C run above ratio 1.2, 0x2B walk, 0x2A slow) comes from that length divided by the walk step, so a tight turn slowed him into the walk animation. The join at 00170374 (lwc1 f6,0x24(sp); its delay slot, lwc1 f1,0(a1), is redone) becomes j NORM (005B2900): in the free walk (+0x6A4 = 0, no block, stick |x|+|y| at least 0x400) it rescales the displacement vector to the length f20 * min(|x|+|y|, 0x1000) / 4096 (f20 = the step speed of the walk / run, which includes the sprint multiplier), so the speed and the animation do not depend on the turn; the direction is unchanged. Remove this section to get the vanilla speed loss back.
patch=1,EE,005B4200,word,8E4806A4
patch=1,EE,005B4204,word,15000040
