patch=1,EE,00175458,word,0816DB60
patch=1,EE,001752FC,word,0816DB64
// ===== Caim: L3 again while sprinting = 25% speed boost that fades over 1 second (needs the constant run speed / L3 sprint section) =====
// While Caim is already sprinting (sprint latch 002F345C was on in the previous walk frame), a new press of L3 (pad byte 0056CD82 bit 1, active low; held-over presses do not count, and the press that starts the sprint does not count) starts a 60 frame boost: the final run speed is multiplied by 1 + 0.25 * frames left / 60, so it starts at +25 % of the current speed (sprint, the 5 second ramp or the super sprint, whatever is running) and fades linearly to nothing over 1 second. The wind burst plays at each boost start, as at the super sprint start: the burst slot is restarted (Caim +0x560 = 0xEE, +0x564 = 0) and the walk timer +0x6A0 is set to 0x3000 so the sprint hook steps it across 0x4000 again next frame. Another press restarts it; it ends at once when the sprint ends. Hook: cave 1 of the sprint section ends with j 0032695C (cave 2: f20 = run speed * m); 0031B678 now jumps to BOOST (005B7800) instead, which does that multiply, applies the boost and returns to 00170204 like cave 2. State words: frames left 005B78F0, L3 last frame 005B78F4, latch last frame 005B78F8. Tuning: 60 frames = addiu at 005B7854, amount/60 = float at 005B7868/005B786C.
patch=1,EE,005B7800,word,4601D502
