patch=1,EE,0031B678,word,0816DE00
// ===== Ground: air dash (L3 in the air = wind burst + air slash + sprint-speed dash; land with the stick forward to keep sprinting; needs the slash jump double jump, free direction in the air, sprint resumes after a roll and super sprint sections) =====
// 2026-10-30: in PRE the word at 005B7C18 is j SPC (005BE340, 005B7C1C nop): after the 2nd R2 slash (0033F6DC != 0) a sprinting Caim (latch 002F345C on) skips the halving of the air speed and momentum, sets the resume flag 0033EDFC (landing with the stick forward keeps the sprint) and restarts the super sprint count 005B1F00 (5 seconds again).
// Air dash: cave AD (005B7900) is put into the jump-state chain (hook 00174FDC -> 0033ED28; the word at 0033ED38 was j DJ2 and becomes j AD, which ends in j DJ2, so the double jump / slash chain runs as before). s1 = Caim, v1 = jump phase [+0x2EC]. Phase 0 (a takeoff, also the double jump re-entry) re-arms the dash (word 005B7AF4). In the takeoff / flight phases (1, 2), a new press of L3 (pad byte 0056CD82 bit 1, active low; edge word 005B79F0, so L3 held through the takeoff does not fire) makes the dash once per jump: the wind burst slot is started ([+0x560] = 0xEE, [+0x564] = 0), the air slash is started like the triple slash does it (FUN_001767A8(Caim, 1), jump type [+0x660] = 1), the air speed word AIRGS (0033EDA8) is set to twice the larger of the current air speed and sprint speed (sprint 1.9 = base run 1.38 x 1.37, so at least 3.8) and the momentum (+0x300 / +0x308) is set to Caim's facing (+0x5B0 / +0x5B8) at that speed; from the next frame the free-direction-in-the-air cave steers it toward the stick at that speed. The roll-resume flag 0033EDFC is set, so in the first walk frame after the landing with the stick forward the sprint latches (AUTOC fakes the L3 press; the wind burst of the sprint start plays) and the super sprint count starts from 0 (takeoff and air attacks zero it). Slower fall: while the dash slash plays (clip [+0x120] == 0xAA and progress [+0x122] < 0x1000; the first 3 frames always; counter 005B7AF8) the downward part of each frame's y change (+0x84, y grows downward; last y 005B7AFC) is halved. It ends when the slash ends or Caim lands. Landing: the flight phase waits for the slash animation to finish, so Caim stayed in the jump state on the ground (states: mode 5, phase 2, y = ground, clip 0xAA progress 0xA50 / 0xD98). Word 005B7AEC now counts the frames since the dash; from the 3rd, when y (+0x84) is within 1 of the ground height (+0x650), AD passes phase 6 on (v1 = 6), which makes FUN_00174FC0 return 1 (finished) at once. The same word marks the dash for the landing: the hook 001737C0 (jal STANDB, right after the mode machine stores the new mode) now goes to LANDC (005B7B20), which in the first frame in the ground mode ([+0x2DC] == 2) clears the word and requests the locomotion animation at once (request block +0x170 = 1, +0x172 = 0x2C run when the stick is out of the dead zone, else 0x21 idle, +0x174 = 0x1000, +0x176 / +0x178 / +0x17A = 0, the default short blend), cutting the rest of the slash animation, then continues into STANDB as before. A takeoff clears the word. PRE (005B7BA0) now sits in front of AD (0033ED38 = j PRE, PRE ends in j AD), skipped in takeoff frames: (1) R1 after a dash: the R1 double jump re-enters the takeoff without AD ever seeing phase 0, so the dash landing stayed armed and cut the R1 jump heavy attack off near the ground. Before a dash PRE records the air speed and momentum (005B7CF0 / CF4 / CF8); when the R1 double jump flag 0013E530 = 0x800 shows up while the dash word 005B7AEC is set, it clears the dash (005B7AEC, 005B7AF8), puts the air speed and momentum back to the pre-dash values (no dash speed in the R1 attack) and clears the sprint resume flag 0033EDFC. (2) Second R2 slash (the slash double jump; 0033F6DC != 0 from it until the next takeoff): the air speed AIRGS and the momentum are halved once, and any later raise in the same jump (e.g. an air dash) is halved again (reference 005B7CFC), so Caim stays at half speed for the rest of the time in the air. (3) While that slowdown is on, every air frame: if the air speed is below 1.85 (normal sprint starts at about 1.89) the sprint ends (latch 002F345C and the resume flag 0033EDFC cleared; Caim lands at the normal run pace and L3 has to be pressed again); at 1.85 or more the sprint continues but the super sprint count 005B1F00 is reset, so the 5 second build-up starts again after the landing.
