// ===== Ground: Square + stick right = the Circle action (stick left / neutral = the Square action) =====
// The game reads Square / Circle for its actions as pressure bytes of the pad copy 00342850 (+0x14 + button index: Circle 9 = 0034286D, Square 0x0B = 0034286F; left stick X at +0x16 = 00342866, 0x00 left, 0x7F centre, 0xFF right). T2 (start of the pad update, before the pad copy is read) jumps to the pad table cleanup at 00321A74 (j 005B6D00, lui t8,0x34 in its delay slot); that jump now goes to SQ (005AF900, ends in j 005B6D00): Square and Circle are the same button: when the left stick X is 0x89 or more, a Square press is moved onto Circle's byte (kept if Circle's is higher) and Square's is set to 0, so the game sees Circle (right dodge); stick left or at rest, a Circle press is moved onto Square's byte the same way, so the game sees Square (left dodge). While Caim rides Angelus on the ground (Caim +0x6B4 = 003ACC94 == 2 and aerial marker 00340DFC == 0) SQ changes nothing, so her Square / Circle dodges are the vanilla L1 / R1 ones. SQ saves T2's t3 / t4 / t6 at 005AF9C0 and restores them before it leaves (the free-direction-in-the-air cave AIRC at 00341C94 tests T2's t3 and t6; without the restore Caim could not turn in the air), and otherwise uses only t3 / t4 / t6 / t9: the cleanup cave 005B6D00 stores T2's t5 through T2's t2 (0x570000, the action table base) and 00321A7C uses t8, so those must stay as T2 left them (an earlier try clobbered t2 / t5 and wrote a stray value every frame, which broke the game).
// 2026-10-28: stick at rest = no remap (Square = left dodge, Circle = right dodge, vanilla); stick pushed = the side decides (x >= 0x80 right). SQ moved to 005BBE00, its saved registers to 005BBFE0.
