// ===== Ground: dodges roll ahead (Caim is turned so the left / right roll carries him the way he was facing) =====
// The roll animation itself carries Caim to his side (changing only the roll's movement vector, as a first try did, had no visible effect). The roll mode FUN_00173E38 reads +0x690 in its first frame for the animation row (00173E98) and the direction (sign bit set = 0xF010 = the right roll). 00173E98 (lhu v1,0x690(s3); the addiu s1 behind it runs in the delay slot) is j TR (005AF600): in the first roll frame (a1 != 0) Caim is turned 90 degrees so the roll's side points the way he faced: right roll -> turn right 90, left roll -> turn left 90 (the first try had them the other way round, 180 degrees off) (yaw +0x44 and rotation yaw +0x584, accumulator +0x204 = 0, +0x570 |= 2 so the roll rebuilds his matrix at 00173F04 before it reads the right axis). Then the lhu and on to 00173EA0. The animation is the roll that was triggered (Square + stick left / neutral = left roll, Square + stick right or Circle = right roll). After the roll the stick-facing section turns him back to the stick at once while it is held. Neutral stick (Caim +0x67C / +0x67E, |x| + |y| < 0x400; Square at rest): turned the other way from the ahead turn for either roll type (the neutral press is the right-roll type, so -90), so the roll carries him straight behind himself whichever way he faces. After the roll: TR sets 005AF8F0 = 1 (rolled), 005AF8F4 = 1 for the neutral (backward) roll and 005AF8F8 = the way the roll travels (his facing before the turn, + pi for the backward roll). The ground-mode handler call 001737C0 (was jal LANDC 005B7B20, the air dash landing cave) is jal RB (005AF300, ends in j LANDC with ra untouched): in the first frame back in the ground mode ([+0x2DC] = 2) after a roll it sets +0x6CC = 1, so STANDB (005B2700, run after LANDC in the same frame) creates the wind burst directly from his matrix (+0x50): after the backward roll 2 frames later (counter 005AF2F4), once his turn is in that matrix, so the burst starts facing the way he does; after a left / right roll only when the left stick is still held at the end (he keeps moving; a left / right roll that ends standing gets no burst); then, with the left stick held forward or back (pad copy 00342866 x / 00342867 y: the vertical part at least 0x30 from the centre 0x7F and not smaller than the horizontal part) it turns Caim to face the way the roll travelled, the way FACE turns him (+0x204, +0x210 |= 2, +0x584, +0x570 |= 1); otherwise after the backward roll it turns him 90 degrees to the right AT ONCE (yaw +0x44 / +0x584 set, +0x570 |= 2, matrix rebuilt with FUN_0012A644(+0x570) as TURNC does; ra / a0-a2 saved in 005AF2E0..EF). (A try that rotated the burst in the burst slot updater at 00178D64 had no effect and was removed.) Block dodge: when the block action is held as the roll starts (Caim +0x66C bit 0x80) TR uses a different rule: the roll goes along the stick direction in the world (x * right axis - y * forward axis, 360 degrees; no stick = straight back), Caim being turned so the roll's side points that way (the 0xF010 roll travels yaw - 90, the 0x0FF0 roll yaw + 90); the animation is the one the Square mapping chose by the stick half (left half = left dodge, right half = right dodge). His facing before the roll is kept (005AF8F8, flag 005AF8FC) and RB turns him back to it in the first frame after the roll, so he keeps guarding the same way; a block dodge gets no wind burst.
// 2026-10-28: rolls now go along the stick direction, pushed out of the 30 degree cones straight forward and straight back to the 15 degree line on the stick side; stick at rest = vanilla roll (no backward roll any more). TR moved to 005BC000 (grew). Generator build_rollahead.py, model test test_dodgecone.py.
// 2026-10-28 b: the excluded cones are 60 degrees wide (30 each side of straight forward / back; CONE_HALF in the generator) and block dodges with the stick pushed use the same clamp (they still remember the pre-roll facing and get no burst; block with the stick at rest still rolls straight back).
// 2026-10-28 c: cones widened to 90 degrees (45 each side of straight forward / back).
// 2026-10-28 d: RB no longer turns Caim after a block dodge (he keeps the facing the dodge left him with).
// 2026-10-28 e: a block dodge with the stick at rest is the vanilla roll of its button (Square left, Circle right), like the normal rolls.
patch=1,EE,005BC000,word,10A00127
