patch=1,EE,001737C0,word,0C16BCC0
// ===== Ground: dodge rolls are not pulled toward nearby enemies =====
// The roll mode FUN_00173E38 steers the roll toward the nearest enemy within 150 units in every roll frame (00174010..00174080: FUN_0016FA38 with radius 150.0, direction to it into +0x32C), which bent the dodges near enemies. 00174010 (lui at,0x4316) becomes beq zero,zero,00174084 (where that block ends) and its delay slot 00174014 lui v0,0x3B (the value the block's last instruction 00174080 leaves for the code at 00174084), so the block never runs and the roll keeps the direction it started with.
patch=1,EE,00174010,word,1000001C
patch=1,EE,00174014,word,3C02003B
// ===== Caim: leans into curves while running (needs the Auto-attack section) =====
// Caim tilts his body towards the inside of a curve while he runs: no tilt going straight, more the sharper he turns, up to a limit. Regular running leans up to about 14 degrees, sprinting (latch 002F345C on) leans more, up to about 23 degrees, and returns to upright more slowly. Not tested in-game. 2026-11-06: the data word D (smoothed yaw change) moved from 005BE900 to 005BE6F0 (DD in build_lean.py; the TILTF words that address it were regenerated).
// 2026-10-30 (v6, roll angle in both blocks): see src/build_lean.py. Rotating the matrix rows after the fact did nothing visible: the game rebuilds the matrix after the pad update cave every frame. A saved state of v5 (roll float [Caim+0x588] = the tilt, model block only) showed the model matrix rebuilt WITH the tilt (right.y = 0.149, forward row unchanged = roll about the forward axis, positive roll = right side down), yet the model did not visibly lean, so the roll is now also written to the actor block ([+0x48]). TILTF (005BE520): the pad update hook 00321A74 goes to TILTF and ends with j 005BD700 (the Auto-attack cave AUTO), so the Auto-attack section has to be ticked. While Caim walks (main state 2, sub state 2, walk timer [+0x6A0] >= 0x200) it takes the change of the model yaw per frame (wrapped to +-pi) times 3.1 (sprint 4.6), limited to +-0.25 (sprint +-0.39), and glides a helper value D (word 005BE900) towards it by 0.25 per frame and the stored tilt (word 005BE1EC) towards D by 0.15 per frame (0.09 while the tilt shrinks, 0.05 when sprinting, so he comes back upright slowly) (two glides in a row; a single glide of 0.35 or 0.12 was jittery); when he is not walking the tilt fades out (x0.88 per frame, x0.92 when sprinting). A hook inside FUN_0012A644 itself stopped the game at start and was removed.
patch=1,EE,00321A74,word,0816F268
// Lean return 2026-11-09: TILTF moved from 005BE520 to 005B8400 (the 4x faster upright correction made it too long). With the left stick at rest (pad bytes 00342866 / 00342867 within 0x70..0x8F) the tilt fades out 4x faster: while not walking the factor m becomes 1 - 4 (1 - m) (0.88 -> 0.52, sprint 0.92 -> 0.68), while still walking the glide back towards upright is 4x faster (capped at 1). Not tested in-game.
patch=1,EE,005B8400,word,3C0C002F
