[Caim: combat, jumps and blocking]
author=Shade
description=Ground combos, auto-attack, jump slashes and double jumps, block specials, spell and arrow blocking, attack speed and damage.
// 23 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Double jump (press jump again while falling) =====
// Cave 0013E208..0013E258 hooked at 00174FDC (jump state FUN_00174FC0). Uses HELD jump bit [0x66C]&0x200 with its own edge detect (prev held at 0013E534); flag 0013E530: 0 available, 0x800 used (set at trigger; cleared whenever [0x2EC]==0 is seen, i.e. on a fresh takeoff - the forced re-entry does not show 0 to the hook). Triggers when [0x2EC]!=0 (airborne/landing phases), jump newly pressed and not yet used; resets [0x2EC]=0 so the normal takeoff runs again.
// Cleanup 2026-10-25: the old copy of this cave at 0013E208..0013E258 was removed. The hook at 00174FDC goes to 0033ED28 and the live double jump code is at 00321FC8, so that copy was dead, and it was written over the sprint-roll cave that the roll hook 001738F0 jumps to (sections "dodge animations" / "sprint resumes after a sprint roll").
patch=0,EE,0013E530,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,0013E534,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,0013E53C,word,00000000
// Spell press stripped in the jump state: cave 0033ED28 (entered from the hook at 00174FDC, then continues in the double jump cave at 00321FC8) clears the spell press bit 0x10 of [Caim+0x670] every frame of the jump state, so the R1 press that starts the double jump cannot reach the attack state's spell finisher (it reads that bit at 0017C9FC..).
