// ===== Block special: R1 right after an L2 block = attack->spell special (needs Input core) =====
// Block special: the player hit-resolution function FUN_00179598 calls FUN_00179954(actor, result) at 00179918 (result 2 = attack blocked with L2). Cave BH (00321C88, hooked by replacing that jal) sets 00321E34 = 50 frames when the result is 2. Cave RS (runs every frame in levels) then watches Spell (R1, press bit 0x10) inside that window: stage 1 sends the actor back to the ground state (main state request [0x2D4] = 2), stage 2 injects a Square press (and releases L2) once the actor is in ground idle (main 2, sub 2), stage 3 injects a Spell press as soon as the attack reaches its running phase ([0x2F8] == 2) which is the game's own attack->spell special; once the game registered the request ([0x6C8] == 2) it sets [0x6CC] to a wrong animation id so the game believes the first attack animation is over and starts the special immediately (the first attack is skipped). While driving the combo the real Spell button is swallowed. State at 00321E38 (stage), 00321E3C (timer).
// Code: BH 00321C88..00321CA4 (hook 00179918), the RS block stages 00321AD0..00321C84 (they end in j 00321CA8). The section "R2 after blocking an enemy attack" hooks into this code and needs it.
