// ===== Ground: normal jump = side jump slash =====
// Jump state FUN_00174FC0: at a grounded takeoff the jump type [Caim+0x660] is 1 (stick sideways, animation entry 0x3E = id 0xAA slash) or 2 (straight, entry 0x3F = id 0xAB chop); the same value is a1 for FUN_001767A8 (li a1,2 at 001751F4, original 24050002; now 1), so every normal jump is the slash. Sprint jumps and the double-jump attack are unchanged.
patch=1,EE,001751F4,word,24050001
// ===== Ground: sprint jump attack = side jump slash =====
// A sprint takeoff (jump type [Caim+0x660] = 3, walk timer [+0x6A0] >= 0x4000) starts its swing with FUN_001767A8(Caim, 2) at 00175230 (animation table entry 0x3F = id 0xAB, the chop). The delay slot li a1,2 at 00175234 (original 24050002) becomes li a1,1, which selects entry 0x3E (id 0xAA, the side jump slash) like the sideways normal jump. The jump heavy attack (R1 in the air) calls FUN_001767A8(Caim, 2) from its own cave and keeps the chop.
patch=1,EE,00175234,word,24050001
// The sprint takeoff then sets the jump type 3 (li v0,3 at 00175238, original 24020003), whose flight / landing code makes the sprint-only effects (hit box and shock on landing, FUN_00170BFC / FUN_00175F54). The type becomes 1, the side jump slash type, so the sprint jump is simply a slash jump. The jump heavy attack sets type 3 in its own cave and is not touched.
patch=1,EE,00175238,word,24020001
// ===== Ground: slash jump double jump (R2 in the air = jump slash, R2 again after it ends = double jump slash; R1 ends the chain; needs the double jump attack section) =====
// 2026-10-30: regular double jump. The word 00342C10 (beq v1,zero,00342C20) becomes j JD (005BDF40; the or t8,t1,t2 in its delay slot still runs). JD: on the takeoff frame (v1 = [Caim+0x2EC] = 0) it clears its used flag (005BDF14) and counts the press as held (005BDF10); in the air, a NEW press of the jump button (held word [Caim+0x66C] & 0x200, edge memory 005BDF10) with the flag unused, the R1 double jump unused (0013E530 == 0) and the slash chain unused (0033F6DC == 0) sets the flag, clears [Caim+0x2EC] (the takeoff runs again, a plain jump, no attack) and goes on at 00174FE4 with v1 = 0; everything else continues at 00342C88 as before. Uses only at / k0 / k1.
// 2026-10-30: a 4th air slash. The chain flag 0033F6DC goes 0 -> 0x800 (2nd slash, double jump) -> 0xC00 (3rd slash, falling: 005B2514 starts the slash without a takeoff) -> 0xE00 (4th slash). 005B2508 (xori t8,v0,0xF00) now compares with 0xE00, so the 0xE00 step also takes the no-takeoff path (it re-entered the takeoff before, a jump), and the stop value at 005B2548 is 0xE00 (was 0xC00), so a 5th press does nothing. The arc height cave scales the arc for every non-zero flag, so the extra slash does not lift Caim.
// The jump attack of the game is not started by the jump but by the attack button held in the air (FUN_00170AD8: [Caim+0x66C] & 8 in the jump mode, tested in the second switch of the jump state at 001751AC; it sets the jump type [+0x660] to 1 / 2 / 3 and starts the swing, clip id [+0x120] == 0xAA, progress [+0x122] < 0x1000). The first R2 press is therefore left entirely to the game. The double jump cave (00321FC8, reached through the spell-press cave at 0033ED28 whose word at 0033ED38 is j 00321FC8) is replaced by cave DJ2 (00342BE0; parts DJ2B at 00342C88 and DJ2C at 00342C30; the word at 0033ED38 becomes j DJ2). DJ2 keeps the R1 jump heavy attack double jump (spell bits 0x30 of the held word, flag 0013E530; possible at any time in the air, before or after the R2 double jump) and adds the slash double jump on the attack button (R2, held bit 0x8, edge detect at 0033F6FC, flag at 0033F6DC = 0x800 when used): a new press in the air, jump type not 0 (the game has started its jump attack; the press that starts it still sees 0), with the R1 double jump unused and the slash double jump used less than twice (the flag at 0033F6DC goes 0 -> 0x800 -> 0xC00: jump slash > double jump slash > triple jump slash), re-enters the takeoff, at the same moments R1 works ([+0x2EC] = 0). The double jump attack section hook (cave DJS, 00342D1C, entered from 001751B4) then starts the slash instead of the chop: FUN_001767A8(Caim, 1) and jump type 1 (when the attack button is still held the game starts the swing itself). After R1 (0013E530 == 0x800) the attack button does nothing. A fresh takeoff clears both flags. The jump slash itself is left as the game / the slash sections make it (animation table rate 0x1800).
