// ===== Ground: Caim attack animations 1.5x (R2 combo) =====
// The ground attack state FUN_0017C14C copies the playback rate of the attack row (FUN_0017E680 / FUN_0017E464(0): halfword 2 of the row, 0x1000 = 1.0) into the animation request [Caim+0x174] at several sites (sh a0 at 0017C3C0 = first hit, sh v1 at 0017C5D0, 0017C71C, 0017C85C = follow-ups); the attack durations and windows are computed from that value afterwards, so scaling it at the store scales the whole attack. Each of the four stores is replaced by jal to a 4-word routine (srl at,reg,1; addu reg,reg,at; jr ra; sh reg,0x174(s2) in the delay slot; = rate x 1.5) at 003419F8 (a0) and 00341A64 (v1); the next instruction of the site runs in the delay slot of the jal, the routine returns behind it. The rate * 5 / 8 variant at 0017C61C is left alone. (First tried x2: too fast.)
patch=1,EE,0017C3C0,word,0C0D067E
patch=1,EE,0017C5D0,word,0C0D0699
patch=1,EE,0017C71C,word,0C0D0699
patch=1,EE,0017C85C,word,0C0D0699
patch=1,EE,003419F8,word,00040842
patch=1,EE,003419FC,word,00812021
patch=1,EE,00341A00,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,00341A04,word,A6440174
patch=1,EE,00341A64,word,00030842
patch=1,EE,00341A68,word,00611821
patch=1,EE,00341A6C,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,00341A70,word,A6430174
// ===== Ground: wider combo window (6 frames) and minimal attack cooldown =====
// In the running ground attack (FUN_0017C14C, case 2) the next attack of a combo is queued ([Caim+0x6C8]) by an attack button press while the clip runs (bit 0x10 of [Caim+0x110] clear); once the clip is over (bit set) and nothing is queued the state ends at once (0017C4EC bne v0,zero,0017C50C, then 0017C518 not queued -> end), so a press a few frames late is lost and the combo restarts. The lhu at 0017C4E4 becomes j GRACE (00321F28, the dead tail of the old cave T; the andi behind it runs in the delay slot and is redone): with the clip over and nothing queued the state now stays in its input part (0017C92C) for up to GRN = 6 frames (word 0033EDF8 counts them, constant GRN in the sltiu) so a press in that time queues the next attack; after that it ends as before. The price is a short wait at the end of every attack (also the last of a combo). It only covers presses late by that margin; presses made while the clip runs are queued as before.
patch=1,EE,00321F28,word,96020000
patch=1,EE,00321F2C,word,3C080034
patch=1,EE,00321F30,word,30420010
