// Cooldown after an attack chain: FUN_00170A94 (attack start) refuses while the float [Caim+0x740] is above 0. The attack state raises it when it ends: to gp[-0x75A4] = 0.4 (lwc1 f1 at 0017C764, original C77CFF1.. = lwc1 f1,-0x75A4(gp)) or to 0.25 (lui at,0x3E80 at 0017C790 and 0017C7B4). They become 0 (mtc1 zero,f1 and lui at,0), so a new chain can start at once.
patch=1,EE,0017C764,word,44800800
patch=1,EE,0017C790,word,3C010000
patch=1,EE,0017C7B4,word,3C010000
// Standing combos (no stick held): when the attack chain has no next attack the state goes to sub-state [+0x2F8] = 3 (recovery) and waits there until the clip is over (bit 0x10 of [+0x110]) before it leaves (0017CBF0..0017CC04: lhu / andi 0x10 / beq v0,zero,0017CCA4, then [+0x2F8] = 0); with a stick direction held the state is left at once (+0x678 upper half != 0 -> sub-state 6), so moving combos had no such wait. The beq at 0017CBF8 (original 1040xxxx) becomes a nop, so the recovery is left in the next frame.
patch=1,EE,0017CBF8,word,00000000
// ===== Ground: R2 combo can start at once after the R1 air attack (needs the super sprint section) =====
// Attack start (FUN_00170A94) refuses while the float [Caim+0x740] is above 0; the jump attack sets it to 0.82 (gp[-0x76D8], FUN_001767A8 start), so after the R1 air attack and its landing the R2 combo could not start for a while. The sprint speed cave SSC (005B1000, in the walk function, belongs to the super sprint section which has to be ticked too) clears [Caim+0x740] in every walk frame while the double-jump flag 0013E530 is 0x800 (set by the R1 air attack, cleared at the next takeoff) and HEON (word 005B1F44, set to 1 by this section) is on. The first walk frame after the landing / the end of the jump state is the first moment the attack can start. In that frame the attack press also goes through: when the attack button is held in that frame, or was held in a landing frame of the jump state (the landing of the R1 attack; cave DJ2B, in the slash double jump section, writes the held bit to word 005B1F48 in frames with [+0x2EC] >= 3), bit 8 is set in the pressed word [Caim+0x670], which the mode machine reads right after the walk frame, so the R2 combo starts the moment the landing is over. The buffer word is cleared when the R1 flag is not set.
patch=1,EE,005B1F44,word,00000001
// ===== Ground: R2 after blocking an enemy attack (L2) = ground sprint attack, same window as the R1 block special (needs Block special and the super sprint section) =====
// The block special of the Controls remap section (cave BH sets the 50 frame window 00321E34 when an enemy attack is blocked with L2; cave RS watches the Spell press (R1, bit 0x10 of [Caim+0x670]) in it and runs a stage machine, stage word 00321E38, timer 00321E3C) gets a second trigger: the hook at 00321AF4 (the lw of the press word) becomes j SPR (005B2400): with the Spell press it continues as before (j 00321B04); with an attack press (bit 0x8, R2 in the game table) in the window it sets stage 4, ends the window and sends the actor back to the ground state ([+0x2D4] = 2) like stage 1 does. The stage dispatch (00321B48, the lw of the stage) becomes j SPD (005B2480): stage 4 waits for ground idle (main 2, sub 2), then injects an attack press (and releases the block bits as stage 1 does), sets CHG (005B1F60) and ends the machine. CHG makes the attack start (FUN_00173C84, decision at 00173CD8: cave SPCK at 005B2160 treats CHG like a walk timer of 0x4000 or more) take the ground sprint attack (FUN_001712E4); the attack start clears CHG and the walk timer at its common end (cave CHGC at 005B2140, hooked at 00173D24). The walk-frame cave NEWC (005B2100, in front of the super sprint cave) no longer clears CHG (the word at 005B2104 is a nop), because a walk frame can run between the injection and the attack start.
// 2026-11-15 removed unused code: 5B2140..5B2180 (nothing jumped, branched or loaded into it; the words were all zero in the original; no fall-through in or out).
patch=1,EE,00173D24,word,0816C9A0
