patch=1,EE,005B2460,word,00000000
// First-load bug fix: the window word 00321E34 held 0xFFB0F94F (game data) after the first load of a map, so the block window looked open for ever and the first R2 (or R1) press became the block sprint attack (or special). SPR now starts with: if the (already decremented) window t2 >= 0x34 it is junk: window = 0 and leave. A genuine window is 50 at most.
patch=1,EE,00321AF4,word,0816C900
patch=1,EE,00321B48,word,0816C920
patch=0,EE,005B1F60,word,00000000
// ===== Ground: R2 combo can start at once after the R2 jump slash too (needs the R1 air attack section and the super sprint section) =====
// Attack start (FUN_00170A94) needs [Caim+0x2DC] = 2, [Caim+0x740] <= 0 and bit 8 of the pressed word [Caim+0x670]; the float [Caim+0x740] is set to 0.82 by the jump attack start (FUN_001767A8), for the R2 jump slash as well. The section 'R2 combo can start at once after the R1 air attack' clears it in the walk frames only while the double jump flag 0013E530 is 0x800 (the R1 air attack), so after an R2 aerial slash the ground R2 was refused for the rest of the 0.82 seconds (state: after an R2 air slash, [+0x660] = 1, [+0x740] = -0.014 once the timer ran out, flag 0013E530 = 0). The branch of the sprint cave SSC at 005B101C (bne v1,zero,005B1054 when the flag is not 0x800) becomes j EXT (005B6D40; the nop behind it is its delay slot): with the flag at 0x800 EXT continues at 005B1024 as before (clears [+0x740], forwards the buffered / held attack press); otherwise it also continues there when the jump type [Caim+0x660] is not 0 (a jump attack was started in this jump: it stays set until the next takeoff), else it goes to 005B1054 as before. So the ground R2 combo starts in the first walk frame after the landing of any jump attack, with the same buffered-press handling as for the R1 air attack.
patch=1,EE,005B6D40,word,14600003
