patch=1,EE,005BAE1C,word,00000000
// ===== Ground: aim spells left / right by turning Caim in place with the stick =====
// The ground spell is sub-mode 6 of the ground state ([Caim+0x2DC] = 6); the mode machine runs it with jal FUN_0017D954 at 0017382C (a0 = Caim, jump table at 005577E0). That jal now goes to wrapper SW (005B7F10), which calls FUN_0017D954, keeps its return value and, while Caim is still in sub-mode 6 and the stick x (short +0x67C in Caim's frame, + = right, range +-4096) is outside the dead zone (|x| > 0x400), turns him in place by x / 4096 * 0.07 rad per frame (about 240 degrees per second at full stick) the way the lock-on FACE routine turns him: +0x204 = step, +0x210 |= 2, chase yaw +0x584 = yaw +0x44 + step (wrapped), +0x570 |= 1. Forward / back on the stick do nothing. With the R3 lock-on on (bit 0 of 00321E2C) SW calls the lock-on routine FACE (00341E00, a0 = Caim) instead, so the spell is aimed at the target. Tuning: the float loaded by the lui / ori at 005B7F7C / 005B7F80 (0.07 / 4096).
