patch=1,EE,0017382C,word,0C16DFC4
// ===== Ground: spell casting 3x faster =====
// The spell sub-function FUN_0017D234 (only called by the spell state FUN_0017D954) sends its animation speed as requests (type 1 / 2, and type 5 = change the speed of the current animation, every frame) by storing a rate into Caim's request block (+0x174, 0x1000 = 1.0). The request is used during the game's own update, so changing +0x174 later in the frame had no effect. Each store now multiplies the rate by 1.5 (3x was too fast; the section name still says 3x so PCSX2 keeps it ticked): 0017D3D0 (sh t0) / 0017D548 and 0017D560 (sh a3) become jal to 4-word routines at 005AF100 / 005AF110 (srl at,r,1 ; addu r,r,at ; jr ra ; sh r,0x174(s0)), the next instruction runs in the jal delay slot; 0017D5F4 (sh v0,0x170 before sh t0,0x174 and a beq) becomes j C5 (005AF120: the two stores with t0 x 1.5, then the beq's j 0017D6F8 with its sw v1,0x2F8 delay slot); 0017D6C8 (beq zero,zero,0017D6F8 with sh v1,0x174 in its delay slot) becomes j C6 (005AF138: the store with v1 x 1.5, j 0017D6F8). An earlier try that raised +0x174 from the widescreen HUD cave was removed.
patch=1,EE,005AF100,word,00080842
patch=1,EE,005AF104,word,01014021
patch=1,EE,005AF108,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,005AF10C,word,A6080174
patch=1,EE,005AF110,word,00070842
patch=1,EE,005AF114,word,00E13821
patch=1,EE,005AF118,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,005AF11C,word,A6070174
patch=1,EE,005AF120,word,A6020170
