// ===== Caim: sprint attack and jump sprint attack deal 10% of the damage =====
// The enemy hit function (FUN_00184A18; s0 = the enemy) asks FUN_00194D80 for the damage of the hit's attack id (halfword [s0+0x18E], a0 of that call; table 00400498, 16 bytes per id) and keeps the result in s1. Measured with an execution breakpoint on 00194D80: both the sprint attack and the jump sprint attack arrive with attack id 0x235 (565). The word at 00184C84 (lhu v1,0x188(s0); its delay-slot partner daddu s1,v0,zero still runs) becomes j 005BDE00: the cave redoes the lhu and, for attack id 0x235, multiplies s1 by 0.25 (FPU, truncating; 2026-10-30: was half, then a quarter, then 10%, then 20%, now 25% - the section name still says 10% because PCSX2 tracks ticked cheats by name; the game raises a zero to 1 afterwards) before going on at 00184C8C. Every other attack is untouched.
patch=1,EE,005BDE00,word,96030188
