// ===== Caim: attacks block enemy spell balls (the block result, no damage) =====
// The player hit function FUN_00179598 (a0 = Caim, a1 = hit record) copies the hit data into Caim and then tests for the L2 block. The word at 00179890 (addiu v0,zero,5) becomes j 005BE100: when the hit's attack id (lhu [s1+0x24]) is 0x28D (the enemy spell ball) or 0x289 (arrow) and Caim is in an attack (main state 2, sub state [+0x2DC] 4 ground / 5 air) the function takes the game's own guard path (s3 = 2, continue at 00179918: FUN_00179954(Caim, 2) = L2 block state with the block callback 001799F8, v0 = 2 = blocked, no damage), but only for hits from the front arc: the projectile's position (hit record +0x80) must be within 135 degrees of Caim's facing (+0x70) for air slashes (270 degree arc) or 120 degrees for ground attacks (240 degree arc); a hit from behind is a normal hit. The attack is interrupted with the block animation, spark, sound and knockback. Arrows are not covered yet. Not tested in-game.
// 2026-11-11: the id test was only 0x28D / 0x289; the arrows in the game are 0x289..0x28C (0x28A seen) and the spell balls 0x28D..0x290, the next family 0x291..0x294: every projectile id 0x289..0x294 now takes the block path (id - 0x289 < 12, words 005BE100..005BE120).
// 2026-10-30: counter attacks. The deflect writes DFB (005BE1F4) = 2 before it enters the guard path; the block special's cave BH ends with j 00179954, now j BH2 (00321CA0 -> 005BE420), which turns DFB 2 into 1 (a deflect block) and clears it for any other call. The R2-after-block cave SPR (005B2430 / 005B2434 -> DFC 005BE460) ignores the attack press while DFB is 1, so a deflect block only allows the R1 special.
patch=1,EE,005BE100,word,96280024
