// ===== Lock-on core: FACE and SEL routines (turn Caim to the nearest enemy; used by the lock-on, spell aim and air attack sections) =====
// FACE (00341E00..00341FE4, a0 = Caim) finds the target through SEL and turns Caim to it the way the game does (yaw-delta accumulator +0x204, flags +0x210 bit 1, +0x584 synced, +0x570 bit 0). SEL (005B8100) clears 005A0904, calls the game's nearest-enemy search FUN_0016FA38 (radius 400) and copies the winner recorded in 005A0904 to 005A0900 (the remembered enemy; 0 = none, which also switches the lock off). The winner is recorded by the hook at 0016FB50 (best-so-far update -> cave 00342024: does the original mov.s f20,f0 and stores the candidate object v1-0x80 in 005A0904). Callers: the lock-on attack wrapper W, the dot DOT, the spell aim cave SW and the air attack wrapper JW.
// Cleanup 2026-10-25: the lock-on wrapper SEL was moved from 003427CC to 005B8100 (FACE 00341E1C and DOT 003420E4 now jal 005B8100) and the sticky-target cave from 00342800 to 005B8140 (hook 0016FAD4 now j 005B8140): both used to sit inside the game sound task object CTaskSound at 00342708.
patch=1,EE,0016FB50,word,080D0809
