// ===== Lock-on: sticky target (the locked enemy always wins the game's nearest-enemy search; needs Lock-on core) =====
// Hook 0016FB3C inside the game's nearest-enemy search FUN_0016FA38 (sqrt of the candidate distance -> cave 00341FE8): while the lock is on, the remembered enemy (005A0900) gets distance 0, so it keeps winning as long as it is alive and in the query. NOTE: FUN_0016FA38 is a game function, so this changes its result for every caller while the lock is on (suspect for the missing-enemy bug).
patch=1,EE,0016FB3C,word,080D07FA
patch=1,EE,00341FE8,word,46000004
