// ===== Lock-on: air attacks face the target (R2 air slashes, air dash slash, R1 air attack; needs Lock-on core) =====
// 2026-10-28: fixed-camera (isometric) stages (Caim +0x6B4 = 4) rewrite the chase yaw +0x584 (camera yaw) every frame, which wiped out the turn FACE asks for. The jal FACE at 005B827C now goes to ISOJW (005BAE40): it calls FACE, and in that mode also copies the yaw FACE just wrote (+0x584) into Caim's facing +0x44 so the air slash turns to the target at once.
// Ground attacks already face the R3 lock-on target (wrapper W calls FACE in the attack state). The jump state (sub-mode 5) is run by jal FUN_00174FC0 at 0017381C; that jal now goes to wrapper JW (005B8230), which calls FUN_00174FC0 and then, while the lock-on is on, Caim is still in the jump state and a jump attack is running (jump type [+0x660] != 0: the R2 air slashes, the air dash slash, the R1 air attack), calls FACE (00341E00, a0 = Caim), so the attack turns to the target. Spells face the target through the spell aim section (SW), sprint attacks run in the ground attack state and already did.
patch=1,EE,005B8230,word,27BDFFE0
