[Camera]
author=Shade
description=Camera behaviour on the ground and in the air, field of view and the lock-on camera.
// 19 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Camera: no auto-recenter =====
// The camera stays where you put it. The stick now MOVES the camera offsets (they add up each frame) instead of positioning them, so releasing the stick, however long you held it, no longer lets the camera ease back. Offsets are limited to +/- pi/2 (the same range as before). Independent of the main cheat.
// Camera update (FUN at 00196DB4). Right stick -> f20 (horizontal) / f21 (vertical), each about +/-pi/2.
// The camera offsets are camera-object 003ADAC0 +0x180 (f20) and +0x184 (f21). Vanilla eases each toward its
// stick target at 1/8 per frame (so releasing the stick eases back to 0 = the auto-recenter):
//   f1 = (target - cur) * 0.125 ; cur += f1                 (cur = f0)
// New: cur = clamp(cur + target * 0.015625, -pi/2, +pi/2)    (a full push sweeps the range in about 1 second)
//   00196FD0/00196FF0 lui at,0x3E00 -> lui at,0x3C80         (rate constant 0.125 -> 0.015625)
//   00196FD8          sub.s f1,f20,f0 -> mul.s f1,f20,f2     (X: step = stick * rate)
//   00196FF8          sub.s f1,f21,f0 -> mul.s f1,f21,f2     (Y)
//   00196FDC/197000   mul.s f1,f1,f2  -> jal 00326968        (shared clamp routine; the following add.s f0,f0,f1
//                                                             runs in the delay slot, and the routine returns to the
//                                                             swc1 / jal that follow)
// Vertical rate (0x180 block, constant at 00196FD0): 0x3CD0 = 0.0254 instead of 0.015625: with the stick value of +-pi/2 a full push moves the pitch offset by 0.0399 rad per frame, the same as the horizontal orbit (right stick X * 0.04 per frame in cave 0013E2A4).
// Clamp routine at 00326968 (padding after a function return):
//   lwc1 f3,-0x7FDC(gp)  (+pi/2 at 00565F14) ; lwc1 f4,-0x7FE0(gp) (-pi/2 at 00565F10)
//   min.s f0,f0,f3 ; jr ra ; max.s f0,f0,f4 (delay slot)
patch=1,EE,00196FD8,word,4602A042
patch=1,EE,00196FF0,word,3C013C80
patch=1,EE,00196FF8,word,4602A842
// ===== Camera-relative movement (also disables controller rumble) =====
// Pushing the left stick forward moves Caim away from wherever the camera points (the stick is rotated by the angle between the camera's right direction and Caim's right direction). Controller vibration is DISABLED because its code is reused for this.
// Caim's movement code turns the stick (x = steer, y = forward) in CAIM's own frame (actor matrix at +0x580,
// right vector = actor+0x590/+0x598). The camera yaw (camera object 003ADAC0, right vector = +0x50/+0x58) is the
// base heading plus the right-stick offset, so we rotate the stick by the angle between the two:
//   C = cR.aR ; S = cRz*aRx - cRx*aRz ; x' = x*C + y*S ; y' = y*C - x*S
// Applied at the end of the player input copy (FUN at 0016EC30, only used for the player; stick shorts live at
// actor+0x67C / +0x67E): 0016ECA0 was "jr ra" -> "j 00149B98".
// Space comes from the rumble system: 00149B90 (rumble table lookup) and 0013E4EC (rumble set) are turned into
// "jr ra ; nop" (vibration off), and their old bodies hold the code:
//   chunk A at 00149B98..00149BD8 (17 words), chunk B at 0013E4F4..0013E52C (15 words).
// If left/right feels mirrored, flip the sign of S: change the sub.s at 00149BC0 (46073181) to add.s (46073180)
// and the add.s at 0013E500 (460A4A40) to sub.s (460A4A41).
patch=1,EE,00149B90,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,00149B94,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,0013E4EC,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,0013E4F0,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,0016ECA0,word,080D0164
// Angelus ride guard: the camera-relative stick rotation reads camera object 003ADAC0, which is not the active camera while Angelus is ridden in a ground stage (identity matrix), so Angelus stopped turning. 0016ECA0 now jumps to GUARD (00340590): when Angelus is being ridden (Angelus actor +0x20 == 5; it is 1 in normal Caim stages) and it is not an aerial stage (3A4 != 3) it skips the rotation AND the ground input cave RS (RS strips the dodge bits 24/25), sets the ground remap word 00321E30 = 30 and clears the aerial marker 00321E34, then returns, otherwise it continues at 00149B98 as before.
patch=1,EE,00340590,word,3C08003B
