// 2026-10-27: the DEBUG camera log (CAMLOG at 005B4400, ring 005B4500) was removed: 005B4400..005B6000 is game memory (the game's own ring of camera records), so the log overwrote game camera data every frame. The cave ends in jr ra again (0013E310).
// ===== Camera: eye azimuth locked to world yaw (no swing in dodges) =====
// Needs "[Camera: world-fixed 360 orbit]". Found with camera logs: the final eye azimuth is az(eased anchor cam+0x110 relative to Caim) + pan [cam+0x184]; the orbit cave set pan = W - (Caim yaw), which is only right if the eased anchor sits exactly behind Caim NOW. The eased anchor lags Caim yaw (1/16 per frame) so any fast turn (dodge spin) swung the eye around him. This hook (jal at 00197000 -> cave 00321840) runs the orbit cave, then recomputes pan = W - atan2(vx,vz) where v = (cam110 + (anchor-cam110)/16) - Caim pos (the eased anchor as it will be after this frame easing), via an inline polynomial atan2. Emulator test: eye azimuth == W within 1e-5 rad.
patch=1,EE,00197000,word,0C0C8610
