// ===== Camera: no special-attack zoom or shake =====
// Special attacks (and other effects that use the camera effect timers) no longer zoom the camera out or shake it. The camera effect words are forced to zero every frame. Independent of the other camera cheats.
// Camera object 003ADAC0 (state comparison before/during a special attack): +0x15C = zoom pulse length (1.5), +0x160 = its elapsed time; the update FUN_00196DB4 pushes the camera back by up to 40 units with sin(+0x160 / +0x15C) while they are non-zero. +0x150 = shake amplitude (counts down; rotation shake matrix at +0xA0..+0xDC, reset to identity only when the countdown ends). All three are zeroed, and the shake matrix is forced to identity, every frame. The cave of the fixed-distance cheat is not involved. 2026-10-30: the per-frame patches alone left one frame of zoom / shake when a special attack finisher started the effect (the game sets the words after the patch ran and the camera update uses them in that same frame). Hook 00196DB4 (first instruction of the camera update FUN_00196DB4, a0 = camera) -> ZCAM (005BEC00): zeroes +0x150, +0x15C and +0x160 at every entry of the update, then runs the replaced addiu sp,sp,-336 and returns to 00196DB8.
patch=1,EE,003ADB60,word,3F800000
