// ===== Ground: wider field of view (0.9, vanilla 0.725) =====
// Wider field of view outside aerial stages: cave T2 (in the pad update) copies the float at 0033F6F8 into the main camera field of view (camera 003ADAC0 +0xF0, vanilla 0.725, set from the constant at 00566F04 / 00566FDC) every frame while the word is non-zero. Value 0.9 = 3F666666 (about 24 percent wider). Change the word to tune. 2026-11-06 (dismount camera): the camera functions set their field of view from two constants every time they run: FUN_001962D4 at 001961CC (lwc1 f0,-28652(gp) = 00566F04, stored to cam +0xF0 at 001961D4) and the second camera function at 00197EB8 (lwc1 f0,-28436(gp) = 00566FDC, stored at 00197EC4); both 0.725 (the only readers). During the dismount jump the live camera (003AD510) read 0.725 and jumped to 0.9 at the landing (user states 1 / 2), because the camera used there takes the constant, which the pad-time copy does not reach. Both constants are now 0.9 (3F666666) as well, so every camera has the ground field of view. Aerial stages keep their own 1.1 (AFOV writes it every frame).
patch=1,EE,0033F6F8,word,3F666666
patch=1,EE,00566F04,word,3F666666
patch=1,EE,00566FDC,word,3F666666
// ===== Camera: no automatic tilt (running, attacking, jumping) =====
// Camera function FUN_001962D4 tilts the view in two ways that the right stick does not control. (1) Speed: [cam+0x144] eases (rate gp-0x6FCC) towards (|Caim movement per frame| / 0.0463 - 15) / 10 (0..1) and adds blend * 10 to the aim offsets and blend * 2.5 * 2pi / 360 to the pitch (the log showed [+0x144] climbing 0.1 -> 0.7 while Caim ran and the pitch following it). The 15.0 is built by lui at,0x4170 at 00196508; it becomes lui at,0x7F00 so the target stays 0. (2) Height: two view angles are int(f * 0.6 - 14) and int(f * 0.3 - 27) with f = y difference between two Caim objects (0 on the ground, -16 in a jump, which tilted the view by about 10 degrees); the slopes are the floats at 00566F10 (gp-0x6FE0, 0.6) and 00566F18 (gp-0x6FD8, 0.3, only used here), both become 0, leaving the on-the-ground angles (-14, -27).
patch=1,EE,00196508,word,3C017F00
patch=1,EE,00566F10,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00566F18,word,00000000
// ===== Camera: pitch only from the right stick or the lock-on (no bob while running / turning) =====
// The log of a quick turn / circling showed the camera pitch ([cam+0x40]) bobbing by about 0.08 rad while the right stick, both offsets and the yaw stayed constant: the camera function integrates a pitch delta (f0 = the look-at pitch correction) into the pitch accumulator each frame (00196A98 add.s f1,f1,f0, f1 = [cam+0x40]), and the correction changes as Caim moves relative to the eased anchor. 00196A98 becomes j PITCHC (005B5600; the lwc1 in its delay slot stays, PITCHC jumps back to 00196AA0): the add is done only when the right stick Y (float at 00342F8C) is above 0.05 in magnitude or the R3 lock-on is on (bit 0 of 00321E2C), otherwise the pitch stays exactly where it is.
// 2026-11-15 removed unused code: 5BB400..5BB448 (nothing jumped, branched or loaded into it; the words were all zero in the original; no fall-through in or out).
// ===== Camera: rigid follow (the camera anchor no longer lags behind Caim) =====
// The camera eye is built from an anchor ([cam+0x110 .. +0x118]) that eases towards Caims position at 1/16 per frame (00196668 lui at,0x3D80 / mtc1 at,f5, used at 001966C8..001966DC). When Caim starts, stops or turns, the anchor lags and trails, so the distance and angle from the eye to him change: the log of a circling run showed the pitch swinging by +-0.1 rad (the pitch accumulator and both offsets stayed constant, my pitch hold had no effect, the look-at pitch comes from this geometry) and a pan offset between -2.7 and -0.4 within 20 frames. The factor becomes 1.0 (lui at,0x3F80): the anchor is Caims position every frame, so the eye keeps a fixed offset (world yaw W, the right stick pitch and distance) from him. The prediction of the eye azimuth cave (00321870, the same /16 for the anchor) gets the same 1.0. Needs the eye azimuth section. Remove this section to get the lagging camera back.
patch=1,EE,00196668,word,3C013F80
// Caim on foot: camera eye 2.5 units higher AND following his jumps (eye only, smoothed, +0 after the double jump): CAME 005BE560 (src/build_caimcam.py), hook 001974C4; the 001966AC anchor hook was removed
