// 2026-11-14 camera tilt: FAST MODE + Cross held on a ground ride tilts the ridden camera forward 20 deg, smoothly (0.025 rad per frame toward the target, current tilt in the free word 005B8A40, 0 = none). CAMY now ends with j 005B8A50 instead of j 00198890: the cave steps the tilt, builds sin / cos with a Taylor series and rotates the camera object forward row (+0x70) and down row (+0x60) about its right axis (fwd = fwd cos + down sin), then j 00198890. Not riding / not a ground stage: tilt word reset to 0.
