patch=1,EE,00198888,word,0816F640
// ===== Camera: vertical pan at constant speed (linear view pitch, same limits) =====
// The pitch offset [cam+0x180] (stepped by the right stick) is turned by the camera into a vertical aim offset (12.73 per rad up, 73.2 per rad down) and the view pitch is the angle to that point, so the same stick speed gave a pitch speed of 0.012 at the bottom, 0.045 in the middle and 0.016 at the top with a kink at offset 0 (log of a full sweep). Settled (offset -> view pitch) pairs from the states: (-1.571 -> -1.127), (-0.904 -> -0.915), (-0.027 -> -0.241), (1.571 -> 0.417). The clamp call of the offset (jal 00326968 at 00196FDC, the add of the step runs in its delay slot) goes to PV (005B5700): it takes cur = f0 - f1 (f1 = the step), maps cur to the view pitch with a piecewise linear fit through those four points, adds the step as an angle (0.0399 rad per frame at full stick, like the horizontal pan), clamps to the same limits (-1.127 .. 0.417 = the old top and bottom) and maps back to the offset the same way; the result is returned in f0. The pitch hold of the earlier section is switched off again (00196A98 = add.s f1,f1,f0): with the rigid camera there is no bob any more, and holding the pitch when the stick was released left the pitch behind the offset (a dead zone when the direction was reversed). Needs the no auto-recenter and the rigid follow sections.
// LOWER LIMIT OF THE CAMERA (look-up end): the last knot is now (1.571 -> 0.029) instead of 0.417 so the eye cannot go below 12 units above the ground (eye y = aim y + 68 * sin(pitch) = -12; the old limit put the eye 13.5 units under the ground, state with the camera clipping the ground). Absolute pitch (cave HP at 005B5B00, hooked in place of the pitch accumulation add.s f1,f1,f0 at 00196A98, its delay slot lwc1 stays, it jumps back to 00196AA0): the view pitch [cam+0x40] is set every frame to the piecewise linear function of the pitch offset [cam+0x180] through the knots (offset -> pitch) (-1.571,-1.127) (-0.904,-0.915) (-0.126,-0.436) (-0.027,-0.241) (0.172,-0.179) (1.571,0.417), taken from settled states. The log showed the settled pitch also depended on Caim running (offset -0.126: pitch -0.436 idle, -0.313 running: the eye elevation followed the lead of the chase frame), so the follower is replaced by this direct mapping: the pitch no longer changes by itself, only by the right stick (or the lock-on, which moves the offset). PV (005B5700) steps the offset with the same knots, so the pitch moves 0.0399 rad per frame at full stick everywhere.
