// ===== Aerial: wider field of view (1.1, ground stays 0.9) =====
// FIX: the writes at 003ADBB0 hit the idle ground camera; the real aerial cameras are CCamAirLForPlayer (003ADC80) and CCamAirHForPlayer (003ADDD0), so AFOV now also stores to 003ADD70 / 003ADEC0 (their +0xF0). In aerial stages (Angelus flying: Angelus actor +0x20 = 5 and +0x3A4 = 3) the pad-update cave T2 (hook 001316E4 -> 00321A20) branches to 00321AC0 (addiu sp,sp,-0x70 / j 00340904 = cave T) before it reaches the ground FOV copy at 00321A78, so the aerial FOV is the one the game sets when the stage loads (0.725 vanilla; a state taken in an aerial stage read 0.9 only because the value was left over from a ground stage). The two words at 00321AC0 / 00321AC4 become j AFOV (005B6100) / nop; AFOV writes the float at 005B6200 (1.1 = 3F8CCCCD, about 62.9 degrees vertical, vanilla 0.725 = 41.5) into the camera field of view (003ADBB0 = camera 003ADAC0 + 0xF0) every frame and then does what 00321AC0 did (addiu sp,sp,-0x70 / j 00340904). Ground stages are not touched (0.9). Change the word at 005B6200 to tune.
