// ===== Aerial: farther camera, AirH/AirL eye offset -300 (vanilla -200) =====
// The aerial cameras (CCamAirHForPlayer / CCamAirLForPlayer, helper FUN_001988e8) place the eye at (0,10,-200) in the target frame: the instruction lui at,0xC348 at 00198960 loads -200.0. 0xC396 = -300.0 (1.5x). Tune: 0xC370 = -240, 0xC3C8 = -400. The earlier 96.0 caves in the ground camera section never ran in aerial stages.
patch=1,EE,00198960,word,3C01C396
// ===== Camera: lock-on camera follows the target twice as fast (needs the lock-on dot section) =====
// The R3 lock-on camera rule in cave DOT turns the camera when the target dot leaves the screen diamond: yaw step = excess px * gain (lui at 005B7350, 0.0021) * z / horizontal distance, pitch step = excess px * -0.0016 (lui at 00342408), each capped at 0.06 rad per frame (lui at 003423D8 / 00342418), and a target behind the camera swings the yaw 0.08 rad per frame (lui at 005B7318). Each float is multiplied by 4 here (exponent + 2 in the lui half; the ori half stays): gains 0.0084 / -0.0063, caps 0.24, behind 0.32 (the section name says twice; kept so PCSX2 keeps it ticked). Placed last so it overrides the original words.
patch=1,EE,005B7350,word,3C193C0A
patch=1,EE,00342408,word,3C19BBCF
patch=1,EE,003423D8,word,3C193E75
patch=1,EE,00342418,word,3C193E75
