// ===== Camera: right stick turning 25% faster (ground) =====
// Right stick camera speed x1.25. Horizontal: the orbit cave (0013E2A4, world-fixed 360 orbit section) multiplies the stick X by gp-0x6E0C (005670E4, 0.04; the game uses that constant elsewhere too, so it is not changed): the lwc1 at 0013E2AC now loads its own word 00342C5C (0.05, zero / unused in every state; at = 0x340000 there). Vertical: the pitch rate lui at 00196FD0 (0.0254, 3CD0) becomes 3D02 (0.0317).
patch=1,EE,00342C5C,word,3D4CCCCD
patch=1,EE,0013E2AC,word,C4222C5C
patch=1,EE,00196FD0,word,3C013D02
// ===== Camera: smooth lock-on camera (no stutter when correcting or crossing up; needs the lock-on dot section and the 2x lock-on camera section) =====
// The lock-on camera rule in DOT applied its yaw / pitch steps directly: in the normal path (00342448: yaw step f6 -> orbit yaw W 0013E538, pitch step f7 -> camera 003ADAC0 +0x180) and in the behind-the-camera path (003421CC: a fixed swing f14 added to W). The steps jump from frame to frame (diamond edge, hard pull, and above all a cross-up that flips the target behind the camera and switches to the fixed swing and back), which made the camera jerk. Both paths now go through FILT (005AF000; the behind path through FA 005AF0A0, which passes f14 as the yaw step and 0 as the pitch step): the applied turn speeds (yaw 005AF1F0, pitch 005AF1F4) move 25 % of the way to the asked step every frame (v += (step - v) * 0.25), so the camera always accelerates and slows down gradually and never changes speed in one frame; then they are added to W and +0x180 and FILT returns to the original continuation (0034246C normal, 00342544 behind). FILT sets 005AF1F8; the widescreen HUD cave zeroes the speeds in frames where it was not set, so a new lock-on starts from rest. Tuning: the 0.25 is lui t9,0x3E80 at 005AF004 (0x3F00 = 0.5 snappier, 0x3E00 = 0.125 softer; a value needing an ori half has to be rebuilt with build_lockcamsmooth.py).
patch=1,EE,005AF000,word,3C08005B
patch=1,EE,005AF004,word,3C193E80
