// ===== Ground: ridden Angelus view uses the ground field of view (story stage transitions) =====
// After a story-mode aerial -> ground transition the ridden Angelus view uses the aerial cameras CCamAirLForPlayer / CCamAirHForPlayer, which kept the aerial field of view 1.1 (sky-coloured bands at the screen sides while riding; gone on foot). The T2 ground path (00321A7C..00321A88 copies the ground FOV word 0033F6F8 to 003ADBB0) ends in j 0033EDAC at 00321A8C; that j now goes to GF (005BAD90), which also stores the ground FOV to 003ADD70 / 003ADEC0 (their +0xF0) when the word is non-zero, then jumps to 0033EDAC. Aerial stages do not take this path. Needs 'Ground: wider field of view'. Must stay after the T2 sections (it overrides the word at 00321A8C, which they set to j 0033EDAC). Generator build_groundfov_air.py. (A version that also stored the ground FOV into five more camera objects on 2026-11-06 did nothing: the states showed all of them at 0.9 while the live camera field of view 003AD510 was still 0.725 during the dismount jump.)
patch=1,EE,005BAD90,word,13200003
