patch=1,EE,00321A8C,word,0816EB64
// ===== Camera: the distance opens smoothly after a dismount =====
// The user's states 1 (last frame of the dismount jump) / 2 (landed) showed Caim larger in the first: the rendered camera during the jump (live camera 003AD4F0) sits 48 units from Caim (40 horizontal) and the on-foot camera, whose arm CAMD holds at 68 (003ADAC0, ground; the loads lui t9,4288 at 005B6330 / 005B6370 in the DA / DB caves), 72 away (66 horizontal), so the view jumped back at the landing (it looked like a field of view change; the field of view words were identical in both states, projection rows 372.6 / 496.8). The two ground loads now go to ARMA / ARMB (005BEE20 / 005BEF00, src/build_armease.py; the mtc1 t9,f9 after the load runs again after the cave): the arm is the word 005BEFFC; while the jump runs (Caim +0x6B4 = 2 and +0x2D0 = 3) it is set to the distance of the live eye (003AD570) from Caim, at most 68; on every other call it eases towards 68 by 7% of the gap per frame, so after the landing the camera opens up from the jump distance to 68 in about half a second instead of jumping. Aerial arms (96) are untouched.
patch=1,EE,005BEE20,word,3C08005C
