[Aerial stages and Angelus]
author=Shade
description=Flying controls, Angelus extras and the ground Angelus ride, the fireball reticle and the terrain height limit.
// 19 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Aerial core: stage detection, pad and input hooks (needs Input core; the other Aerial and ridden-Angelus sections need this) =====
// Split out of the old "Aerial (Angelus) stages: separate controls ..." section on 2026-10-27 (backup BEFORE_split_aerial_2026-10-27.pnach). Aerial stage = Angelus actor +0x30 == 1 and +0x3A4 == 3.
// Input hook 0013E528 -> AERRS (00340544): in an aerial stage it sets the aerial marker 00340DFC = 30, switches the ground lock-on off (00321E2C = 0) and returns; otherwise it clears the marker and jumps to RS (00321A10, Input core). Pad-update hook 001316E4 -> T2 (00321A20): aerial -> AER (00340904), otherwise the ground path (D-pad table writes when that section is ticked, then the T2 placeholder chain other sections use: 00321A74 / 00321A8C / 00321A94 / 00321A9C, and RIDE for a ridden Angelus when that section is ticked). AER counts the marker down and (with the sections below) changes the aerial button table and runs XL. The pad hook 00131AFC -> 003409B4 is the chain the jump heavy attack, ridden Triangle turn and longer dodge sections hook into; it also holds the aerial Triangle U-turn (SHIFT2: both dodge actions while Triangle is down in aerial stages).
patch=1,EE,001316E4,word,080C8688
