// Fast mode: L3 cancels the boost 2026-11-10 (LP in build_glideboost.py, hook 001C09DC now -> LP 005BC680 -> PRE 005BCD80 -> 001C3EBC): in fast mode (toggle word 005BEE0C == 0) the L3 press edge (the glide start) sets the boost multiplier +0x3DE8 / +0x3DEC to 1.0, divides the glide momentum M (005BEFE0..E8) by the old multiplier (the glide starts at the normal speed) and sets LOCK (word 005BEDE4); while LOCK is set the L2 held bits of the pad struct are cleared (no boost, and GBL gives no glide pose), until the L2 pressure drops below 0x40, so L2 has to be released and pressed again. L3 previous state word: 005BEDE0. Standard mode clears the lock. UPDATE: the glide momentum M is no longer divided by the old multiplier: the glide carries the boost speed for its whole run (the boost itself is cancelled at once and stays locked until L2 is released).
