// 2026-11-14 the right stick brake cancels the boost and its animation; a fresh boost press cancels the brake: BRK (005B6E40, entered from 005BC6E0 in LP, the lui there is redone inside it) in fast mode keeps three words: BOK (005B6FF8) = 1 while the right stick is down and the brake is not cancelled (XCB1 / XCB2 now test it: t1 = BOK == 0), CAN (005B6FF0) = 1 once L2 is pressed fresh (down now, up last frame, word 005B6FF4) while the stick is down: the boost cancels the brake until the stick is released; and while the brake is on it sets the boost lock LOCK (word 005BEDE4, the lock of the L3 cancel: LP clears the L2 held bits and GBL / GB2 give no glide pose) which clears itself when L2 is released. Untested.
