// R3 brake mode: right stick moves Angelus, right stick camera off (2026-11-10, src/build_strafe.py + build_aerialboost.py): while the ground brake toggle (R3, word 005BEE0C) is on, GMOV (the ridden ground mover) computes f13 = |n| (her normal cruise movement this frame) and jumps to STRAFE (005BC800) after storing the movement: the right stick (raw pad bytes 00342864 x / 00342865 y, 0x7F centre, dead zone 24) adds a movement of that speed in the held direction relative to her heading (right axis +0x0 / +0x8, forward axis +0x20 / +0x28; strength min(1, |stick| / 100)), and the processed camera stick floats 00342F88 / 00342F8C are cleared every frame in that mode. TILT (005BC900, hook 001C5318 in FUN_001C3EBC) adds rx / 128 * 0.35 to her bank target f24 (the left stick gives stick x * 0.75) so she leans slightly towards the held stick. Untested in-game: whether the camera really stops depends on the order of the pad read and the camera read within a frame.
