// 2026-11-13: the static patch line for 005A07A0 (red 802030F0) was removed: PCSX2 re-applies patch lines every frame, and it raced with SWAP (005BC9A0), which writes the reticle colour (white in brake mode, red otherwise) in the pad update, so the star showed red for a frame about every 6 seconds. The word is written by SWAP only.
// Brake mode 2026-11-10: (1) the steering stick (right stick, swapped into the left slot) has its up / down inverted: SWAP (005BC9A0) now also does 00342867 ^= 0xFF. (2) Strafing no longer turns her: the heading changes by the turn rate +0xB0 / 40, and +0xB0 follows the bank (+0xB4, where the strafe tilt is added to the target f24) at 8% per frame, so the tilt also turned her. TILT stores the tilt it applied in word 005BEE14 (TV); hook 001C470C -> YAWFIX (005BCA40) filters it the same way (word 005BEE18, 8% per frame) and subtracts it from the turn rate before the heading step, so the tilt only banks her; the steering stick still turns her.
patch=1,EE,001C470C,word,0816F290
