// Brake mode 2026-11-10: (1) the reticle core is WHITE (RGBAQ word 005A07A0 = 80FFFFFF) while the brake toggle is on, red 802030F0 otherwise: SWAP (005BC9A0) writes it every ground pad update. (2) L3 dodges in brake mode: GMOV (the L3 glide start is skipped while the toggle is on) jumps to DOD (005BCB00) on the L3 press edge, which sets the dragon dodge buffer +0x3DC4 (left) or +0x3DC8 (right) to 5 frames like the dodge buttons (ride code 001C4E44..001C4E6C); the side is the strafe stick x (raw 00342864 < 120 = left, else right). (3) The dodge direction (DRT 005BCC00, build_angdodge.py: movement along the stick angle with the forward / back cones pushed out to 45 degrees) reads the strafe stick (00342864 / 65) instead of the left stick while the toggle is on, so a held diagonal gives a diagonal dodge. (4) 2026-11-10 later: L2 no longer clears the brake toggle (the NL2 block of GMOV was removed): in brake mode the L2 boost works with the strafe, because STRAFE adds the strafe stick movement at the game cruise speed |n| (f13), which is the boost speed while L2 is held; the brake still holds her forward movement, so she only moves where the strafe stick points. Only R3 turns the mode off now. (5) The right stick camera input (floats 00342F88 / 8C) is now cleared every frame while Angelus is ridden on the ground, also outside brake mode (STRAFE clears them before it tests the toggle).
