patch=1,EE,005B8738,word,0816FA7C
// 2026-11-14 LATEST: in fast mode the brake comes from the RIGHT STICK pushed down (XCB1 / XCB2 test the byte 00342865 >= 0xC0, the forced not braking ori is a nop again) and the same stick position also locks the height (NDC at 005B6710), as does Cross (which no longer brakes). // 2026-11-14 LATER: Cross no longer brakes in fast mode at all (XCB1 / XCB2: ori t1,t1,1 forces the not-braking test), it only keeps her from losing height (NDC). EARLIER: holding Cross prevents descending; L2 overrides the brake. XCB1 / XCB2 (005B8700 / 005B8720) treat a held L2 (t5 = L2 pressure >= 0x40) as "Cross not pressed": with Cross and L2 held (in either order) there is no brake and the boost works; Cross alone brakes as before (fast mode). The ridden ground dragon is moved by the mover 001B77E0: 001B7820 stores the position (sqc2 vf4,0(a0), a0 = dragon + 0xD0) and 001B7824 (sqc2 vf0,0(v1)) clears the movement vector. 001B7824 now jumps to NDC (005B6B30), which clears the vector (the replaced instruction), then for the dragon 0041BFC0 on the ground (marker 00340DFC = 0, Caim +0x6B4 = 2) remembers her y of the last frame (float word 005B6B28; y at dragon + 0xD4, positive down). While Cross (0034286E >= 0x40) is held, a new y greater than the remembered one (descending) is replaced by the remembered y, so nothing can lower her (brake, boost, glide, gravity); climbing and level flight are free. Cross not held: in free mode the remembered y just follows her; in FAST MODE (2026-11-14) she can only descend while the left stick is pushed to aim down (raw 00342867 < 0x68, the value the aiming down input gives); with the stick neutral or pushed up every descent is clamped (aiming down once no longer keeps her sinking, nor the boost, the glide or gravity), otherwise the remembered y follows her. The compare is an integer sign test of (new y - remembered y) after nops: a float compare right after the load skipped the clamp on every second frame in the earlier states. Untested.
patch=1,EE,001B7824,word,0816D9C4
