// Ground boost speed 2.5x 2026-11-10 (src/build_boostspeed.py): the ridden ground dragon update FUN_001C3EBC (tools/decomp_1c3f04.txt) sets, while L2 is held, the target multiplier dragon +0x3DEC = the float at gp-0x626c (00567C84 = 1.8) with the ease rate +0x3DF0 = 0.08; a fresh press first jumps the current multiplier +0x3DE8 to 4.5 (gp-0x6270), which then eases to the target. Hook 001C4D38 -> BST (005BCB40) loads 2.5 instead of 1.8 outside brake mode (word 005BEE0C == 0); brake mode now uses 1.7 (BRAKE_MULT in the builder). (The first version hooked 001C3578, the same code in another function the ground ride never runs, and changed nothing; that word is back to C7809CCC.) MULT in the builder.
// No scripted camera swing on the ridden ground R1 special 2026-11-10 (src/build_nospeccam.py): FUN_0017EC04 (the special start) calls the camera transition setters once on the riding camera object 003ADC80: 0017EC60 jal 00199274 (a1 = 1, f12 = 1.0) and 0017EC78 jal 0019925C (a1 = 1, f12 = 5.0, sets +0x114 = 1, +0x118, +0x11C = 5.0, +0x120 = 0), after which the camera blended towards a look-at target (+0xE0..) and rotated about her (+0x114 went from -1 to 1 and +0xE0 jumped in the user states of 2026-11-10). On a ground stage (marker 00340DFC == 0) the two jal are redirected to CS1 / CS2 (005BCBC0 / 005BCBE0) which return at once (the delay slots have run); aerial stages tail-call the original setters. Undo: 0017EC60 = 0C06649D, 0017EC78 = 0C066497.
patch=1,EE,005BCBC0,word,3C180034
