// ===== Aerial: Angelus cannot fly into mountains (terrain height limit) =====
// Angelus' real position is integrated by the generic actor mover FUN_001B73C0 (position +0xD0 of the actor pose block at 0041BFC0, velocity added, bounds clamp FUN_001B7D70, final store sq t6,0(s3) at 001B77BC); the game's camera, HUD and guidance all read that position through the setter at 0017FA54. The word at 001B77BC becomes j TERC (005B6400); the instruction in its delay slot (ld s0,0x30(sp)) still runs, TERC redoes the sq t6,0(s3), then (only when s3 = 0041C090 = the Angelus pose block, in aerial stages: Angelus actor 003ACF20 +0x20 = 5 and +0x3A4 = 3) looks up the game's terrain heightmap (grid header 00409E70, 160-unit cells, offset 40960, 4x4-cell blocks, 5x5 byte heights per block, scale -5.0 at 00409F90; the data the fireball uses to explode on mountains) at the current x/z AND at the point 10 frames ahead (position change since the last frame, saved at 005B6700 / 005B6704), takes the highest terrain of the two, subtracts the clearance (lui at,0x42C8 = 100.0) and, if she is lower than that, lifts her y by 18 percent of the excess per frame (at least 4.0 units, never above the target), so the climb is smooth and starts before the mountain. The same cave also writes 0 to the y maximum of the pose block's movement bounds (0041C0E4, was -821.0; s3+0x54) every frame, which is what stopped her descending below about y -600; so in aerial stages she can fly down to the ground, and the terrain limit above keeps her over mountains. y is negative = up, so the clamp only ever lifts her; the old flat floor (about y -600) still limits how low she can fly. Tune: the 3E38 51EC word pair = lift fraction 0.18; 4080 = minimum 4.0 per frame; 4120 = 10 frames lookahead; 42C8 = clearance 100.0.
patch=1,EE,005B6400,word,7E6E0000
patch=1,EE,005B6404,word,3C080042
patch=1,EE,005B6408,word,2508C090
patch=1,EE,005B640C,word,16680043
