// ===== Aerial: Angelus fireball speed x2 =====
// Fireball projectile speed doubled. The projectile object (found in save states, the fireball node at +0xD0 position) holds current speed / max speed 46.296 / blend 0.05 and eases cur += (max - cur) * 0.05 each frame (about 25 -> 46 units per frame, speed = trail sample spacing). The values come from a parameter table: max speed 46.296 (42392F67) at 00569430, 00569470 and 005696AC, start speed 23.148 (41B92F67) at 005696A4. Max speed now 92.59 (42B92F67), start speed 46.30 (42392F67). Which of the three max-speed entries is the player fireball was not proven, so all three are changed.
patch=1,EE,00569430,word,42B92F67
patch=1,EE,00569470,word,42B92F67
patch=1,EE,005696AC,word,42B92F67
patch=1,EE,005696A4,word,42392F67
// ===== Ground: Angelus fireball reticle (white dot where the fireball lands while Caim rides Angelus; needs the lock-on dot section) =====
// While Angelus is ridden in a ground stage (Angelus actor 003ACF20 +0x20 = 5 and +0x3A4 = 2; dismounted she has 1/1, aerial stages have +0x3A4 = 3) the lock-on dot cave DOT (003420B0) draws its dot where a fireball fired right now would land, instead of at a locked enemy, and the lock-on camera rule is skipped. Aim model (measured on fireball objects in save states: a fireball object keeps its start point at +0x130 and its constant velocity at +0x120): the fireball starts at her mouth point (ext point 0 of the dragon, 0041CF20 = x,y,z) and flies in a straight line at 8.57 units per frame along her body forward vector (actor +0x70/+0x74/+0x78, y positive = down) pitched down by a fixed 18 degrees (level shots drop 0.309 of the speed per frame; shots fired while she climbed 14.3 degrees drop 0.067, which is exactly 18 - 14.3 degrees), until it reaches y >= 0 (flat ground, the game's own fireball code explodes at y >= 0) or has flown 130 frames (the fireball lifetime; then the dot sits where it would die in the air). RIDE computes the per-frame step from fy and cos(pitch) = |(fx,fz)|: horizontal = speed * (cos18 - fy * sin18 / cos pitch), vertical = speed * (fy * cos18 + cos pitch * sin18). It updates every frame, so the dot follows her aim in real time. While riding, the camera object 003ADAC0 that DOT normally projects with holds only the field of view (its matrix is the identity), so RIDE loads t0 = 003AD4F0, the live camera block (+0x50 right, +0x60 down, +0x70 forward, +0x80 position; same layout), and jumps into DOT's projection at 00342120 with f2/f3/f4 = target x / y - 10 / z. Hooks: 003420C8 (the lock test beq) -> RIDE 005B7000, which falls back to the original lock test when not riding; 003421AC -> BEH 005B7300 (target behind the camera: hide the dot instead of swinging the camera); 003423C4 -> CAM 005B7340 (skip the camera pull while riding). Flag word 005B7F00 = riding. Tuning: the float word pairs in RIDE (8.57 speed, cos / sin of 18 degrees, 130.0 frames). STAR SHAPE: while riding, the dot is replaced by a red three-bladed star like the aerial lock-on reticle, without its orange dots. The star is a second copy of the dot GIF packet at 005A0600 (colours: dark outline 80000000, red fill 802030F0) with its own triangle-fan offset tables at 005A0900 / 005A0980 (center, then tip down, inner, tip up-left, inner, tip up-right, inner, tip down closing, padded with repeats; each entry = (y << 16) + x in 1/16 pixel). Three more hooks in DOT: 003424B8 -> SEL 005B7400 (when riding: table base t8 and the two vertex bases t3 / t2 point at the star copy), 0034251C -> TAG 005B7480 (the chain tag points at 005A0600 instead of 005A0000), 00342560 -> UND 005B74C0 (hiding also accepts the star address, so the chain end tag is restored). Not riding: everything uses the round dot as before. The first word of every vertex qword of the star packet (005A0670 + 16 i, 005A07B0 + 16 i) is written by DOT every frame, so it has no patch line (a patch line there froze the star at a stale position). MOUNTED CHECK: besides the Angelus fields, RIDE also requires Caim (003AC5E0) +0x6B4 = 2, which holds in every riding state and is 1 on foot (found by comparing riding and walking save states). Do not test Caim +0x668: it is 1 only while the stick is neutral and made the reticle vanish when the stick moved. FADE CHECK: RIDE also requires the screen fade to be fully clear (CFadeMan 004861A8, fader value at 004862CC = 0; it is 0xFF while the loading screen is black and counts down while it fades in), so the reticle appears only after the stage has faded in. LEVEL CHECK: the actors keep their riding fields after the stage ends, so RIDE also requires the title, chapter map, result, title call and weapon select tasks (003B9770 003B98B0 003B93B8 003B9640 00342E38) to be inactive, as the HUD cave does; otherwise the star showed on the chapter map. PAUSE CHECK: first of all, while 004EE29C != 0 (pause menu opening / open, also mission briefing) RIDE clears the riding flag and takes DOT's own no-target path (0034253C), so no dot or star is linked and the pause menu text is not cut off.
