// 2026-11-14: the neutral aim is now 16 degrees below her body forward in both modes (13, 9.8 and vanilla 19 before): the FX constant is -0.12217 + 3 degrees; the reticle words are those of 16 degrees. (Earlier the same day it was 13 degrees:) the fireball effect pitch constant in FX (005BD9D4 / D8) is -0.12217 + 6 degrees = -0.01745 (was +9.2 degrees = 0.0384) and the reticle cos / sin words in RIDE (005B70F0..7100) are those of 13 degrees. // Fireball aim raised by 8.2 degrees (2026-11-10): the fireball effect is spawned by FUN_0017EA0C (called from 001C1134), which sets the Euler pitch of the effect block to the constant -0.12217 (lwc1 f2,-29996(gp) at 0017EABC, only user of it; the measured flight is body pitch + about 18 degrees down). On ground stages (marker 00340DFC == 0) the hook 0017EABC -> FX (005BD9C0) loads -0.12217 + 8.2 degrees = 0.02095 instead, so the fireball flies 8.2 degrees higher. SIGN NOT VERIFIED (assumes negative = down); the reticle (RIDE cave constants cos / sin of the pitch at 005B70F0 / 005B70FC) now uses 18 - 8.2 = 9.8 degrees to match. Aerial stages are untouched. Measure with a state that has a fireball in flight: trail pitch minus body pitch should be 9.8 degrees (it was 18.5). CALIBRATED 2026-11-10 with state 9: the sign was right (the flight went from 19.0 to 10.85 degrees below the body, measured on the trail samples: reduction 8.15 for 8.2 asked), but the real base offset is 19.0 not 18, so the effect pitch is now -0.12217 + 9.2 degrees = +0.0384 (real offset 9.8 = the reticle model).
