// Star reticle smoothing 2026-11-09: the two shape tables (005A0904 outer, 005A0984 inner; vertex 0 of each fan is the template origin) are rounded (Chaikin corner cutting of the 6 corner star -> 12 points, then the closing point and padding). The outer fan is no longer a black outline: it is a translucent soft halo (PRIM 005A0650 = 0245 with ABE, colour 005A0660 = A 30 / R C0 G 20 B 20, 1.3x the old outline size, ALPHA_2 = 0x44 = Cs As + Cd (1 - As) written in the packet slot that held SCISSOR_2 (005A0640 / 48; the full screen scissor 0..639 x 0..479 it set is the game default for the 2D layer)). The red core (005A0984 table) keeps its opaque fan. Size is 0.5 of the original (outer 0.65). Not tested in-game; to undo restore BEFORE_starsmooth_2026-11-09.pnach. Update: the three tips are sharp again (original points); only the two inner valleys per side are corner-cut (30%), and the outer ring is a translucent black outline (005A0660 = 60000000). Symmetric redraw: both shapes are exact 3-fold symmetric stars (tip 0 down, tips at 90/210/330 degrees; outline tip radius 150 / valley 30, core 100 / 18 in 1/16 px), sharp tips, valleys rounded with a quadratic curve (4 points each). Symmetric redraw: both shapes are exact 3-fold symmetric stars (tip 0 down, tips at 90/210/330 degrees; outline tip radius 150 / valley 58, core 100 / 38; fatter arms 2026-11-10 so one pixel of rounding does not make a thin tip look shorter in 1/16 px), sharp tips, valleys rounded with a quadratic curve (4 points each). Symmetric redraw: both shapes are exact 3-fold symmetric stars (tip 0 down, tips at 90/210/330 degrees; outline tip radius 150 / valley 42, core 100 / 28; fatter arms 2026-11-10 so one pixel of rounding does not make a thin tip look shorter in 1/16 px), sharp tips, valleys rounded with a quadratic curve (4 points each). Symmetric redraw: both shapes are exact 3-fold symmetric stars (tip 0 down, tips at 90/210/330 degrees; outline tip radius 150 / valley 42, core 100 / 28; fatter arms 2026-11-10; 2026-11-10 later: x squeezed to 0.8 (the 2D layer is stretched about 1.25x horizontally on a 16:9 screen, so the star came out wide) and radii x0.9 (135/38, 90/25) to match the redo.png reference so one pixel of rounding does not make a thin tip look shorter in 1/16 px), sharp tips, valleys rounded with a quadratic curve (4 points each).
patch=1,EE,005A0650,word,00000245
