// ===== Aerial: boost = dive pose with a smooth change (not while climbing), 20% faster in the climb; ground: Cross brakes and L3 glides the ridden Angelus =====
// While the boost action is held (pad action word 00342898 bit 0x100), only for the dragon animation object (s0 == 0041C140) on aerial stages (marker 00340DFC != 0): the pitch parameter read at 001C8728 (FUN_001C868C blend setup; p = 0.5 - 0.5 x pitch in radians, the game takes the dive clip 28 when p < 0.3) is 0.0, so the wings-out dive animation plays (cave BGL 005BED00, src/build_aerialboost.py). Not while she climbs steeply: forward y (dragon +0x24, y points down) below -0.2827 = -sin(0.2866 rad = 16.42 degrees), the climb angle of the user's state 2 (it was 60, 36.46, then 45 degrees earlier on 2026-11-06), up to her maximum climb of 57.3 degrees (pitch +0xC4 / +0xC8 = 1.0 rad), where the normal boost animation plays. The wing wind effect caves (2026-11-06) were removed again, the user did not like the effect (build_aerialboost.py.bak_wind). Climb speed (2026-11-06): cave MOV (005BED5C, hook 001B73F4 in the collision move FUN_001B73C0; the world movement vector is at the dragon + 0xF0) multiplies the movement by 1.2 (CLIMBSPEED in src/build_aerialboost.py) for the dragon on aerial stages while the boost is held and she climbs above 16.42 degrees (the same forward y < -0.2827 test, the range where she flaps normally, up to her climb limit). Smooth pose change (2026-11-06): the pitch parameter the blend setup sees is not switched to 0.0 at once any more. While the boost is held (dragon, aerial stage) a smoothed value SP (word 005BEFF8) moves towards the target by 7% of the gap every frame: target 0.0 (dive pose) normally, the real parameter while she climbs above the climb angle (flapping); the game's own blend weight of the dive pose is 1 - p / 0.3 below p = 0.3, so the wings now change gradually (about half a second) instead of snapping from flapping to the glide when she leaves the climb zone, and the other way round. Not boosting: p as it is (SP follows it). A boost-cancel cave (CANC, hook 005B6100) was tried the same day and removed (build_aerialboost.py.bak_cancel2). Ground brake with momentum and L3 glide (2026-11-06): the ridden ground Angelus is moved by the non-collision mover 001B77E0 (write breakpoint on her position 0041C090: pc 001B7820, ra 001B7808). Cave GMOV (005BE824, src/build_aerialboost.py), hook 001B7810 (addiu v1,s0,240; v1 = the movement vector +0xF0 that the following vadd adds to the position): ground stage (aerial marker 00340DFC = 0), dragon (0041BFC0), Caim riding her (Angelus actor 003ACF20 +0x20 = 5 and +0x3A4 = 2). Every free frame the movement vector n is stored as the momentum M (words 005BEFE0 / E4 / E8) and the L2 boost button held (pad pressure byte at 00342864 + the index byte 005747BA) as the boost flag (bit 0 of word 005BEFEC; bit 1 = L3 was held last frame, bit 2 = L2 was held). The movement is n (1 - w) + M w with the weight w (word 005BEFF4). CROSS (pressure byte 0034286E = 00342864 + 0xA >= 0x40): M is multiplied by 0.93 every frame (0.975 if she was boosting), w rises by 35% of the gap per frame: she slides on in the direction she was going before, whatever she does, longer after a boost. L3 (pad byte 0056CD82 bit 1, active low): on the press edge the glide frames (word 005BEFF0) are set to 120 (2 seconds at 60 movement updates per second; 180 / 3 s until 2026-11-06); on every frame with frames left w = 1 and M stays as it was when L3 was pressed (cruise or boost movement): her direction and speed are locked whatever she does (turning, attacking). Only a FRESH L2 boost press (button down now, up on the last frame; a boost already held when L3 is pressed does not count) or a fresh dodge (the ground ride code, 001C4E44..001C4E6C, buffers a dodge press for 5 frames in the dragon words +0x3DC4 / +0x3DC8 when the action bit 0x01000000 / 0x02000000 of its pad pointer is set; the cave reads those two words, the first version read the pad word 0034289C, which is not the word the ground dodge reads, so the dodge animation played but the locked movement was not cancelled) ends it at once (w = 0, M = n, the boost / the dodge takes over). If the 120 frames run out uninterrupted the RAMP-DOWN starts (flag bit 4 of 005BEFEC): w stays 1 and M is multiplied by 0.93 every frame (0.975 after a boost) until |M| < 1 (a full stop), then w falls by 12% per frame and the normal movement (cruise speed) takes over; a fresh L2 or dodge during the ramp-down ends it at once as well. Pressing or holding L3 again during a glide or its ramp-down does nothing. Only the movement changes: attacks, dodges and the other actions are untouched, the gait animation keeps playing. Brake and dodge (2026-11-06): a fresh dodge while Cross is held ends the brake slide too (w = 0, the dodge movement is the normal one); the brake then stays off (flag bit 5 = 0x20 of 005BEFEC) while the dodge lasts (the dodge timer +0x3D7C, set to at least 15 by the dodge start at 001C4E98..001C4EB4 and counted down by the dragon update 001C550C, or a buffered dodge press in +0x3DC4 / +0x3DC8) and is back at once when it is over, as long as Cross is still held (until 2026-11-06 it stayed off until Cross was let go and pressed again). The lean data word D moved from 005BE900 to 005BE6F0 (build_lean.py DD) so that the caves BGL / MOV / GMOV could use 005BE700..005BEB50 in one piece.
// DODGE DIRECTION (cave DRT 005BCC00, build_angdodge.py; GMOV jumps to it after its riding checks and it returns to GMOV label CONT): while the dragon dodge timer (+0x3D7C) runs, the sideways part s of the movement vector (n . right axis +0x0/+0x8) is redirected like Caim's stick-angle rolls: n' = n - s right + |s| (ux right + uf forward) with (ux, uf) the raw stick (pad bytes 00342866 x / 00342867 y) in her frame; inside the 90 degree cones straight forward / straight back it is pushed out to the 45 degree line on the stick side (x = 0 counts as right); stick at rest (|x|+|y| < 16) = the vanilla sideways dodge of the button. Each dodge button keeps its own side (the sign of s; animation unchanged): a stick held to the other side is mirrored (ux = |ux| on the button side); same distance. Not tested in-game.
patch=1,EE,005BE700,word,C6400000
