// ===== Aerial: Angelus climb limit 58.2 degrees (the user state 1; vanilla 57.3) =====
// Her pitch angle (dragon +0xC4 / +0xC8, radians, up positive) is held between a ceiling and a floor in the dragon object: +0x4238 = ceiling, vanilla 1.0 rad = 57.3 degrees up; +0x423C = floor, vanilla -1.0 rad = 57.3 degrees down. The aerial flight function FUN_001C1BCC stores the ceiling every frame in the delay slot of the branch at 001C2C2C (001C2C30 swc1 f1,16952(s1)), f1 from lui at,3F80 / mtc1 at,f1 at 001C2C14 / 001C2C18; the pitch is eased near the limits (001C2C64, 001C2D08) and clamped against them (001C6810 .. 001C6908, asin of the forward vector). 001C2C14 becomes lui at,3FC0 (1.5 rad = 85.9 degrees; original 3C013F80), so the ceiling is 1.5: she climbs to nearly vertical but cannot go over the top into a loop (a ceiling of 10 with a floor of -10 let her loop and broke the camera, reverted on 2026-11-06). The dive floor is unchanged. 2026-11-06 (later): the ceiling is now 1.015625 rad = 58.2 degrees (lui at,3F82 at 001C2C14, the angle of the user state 1: pitch 1.0164 rad), the 1.5 rad / 85.9 degrees version is replaced.
patch=1,EE,001C2C14,word,3C013F82
// Much faster ground Angelus turning 2026-11-10: the yaw of the ridden Angelus changes by (turn rate +0xB0) / 40 per frame (FUN_001C3EBC, 001C471C lui at,4220 = 40.0; the second path divides by 22.0, 001C47F8 lui at,41B0). The divisors are now 26.6 (0x41D5) and 14.6 (0x416A): 1.5x faster (2x with 20 / 11 was still too much) (5x with 8.0 / 4.5 was too much) heading change at the same lean (the lean +0xB4 is the stick x 0.75 and must not be scaled: 1.5 rad is a 90 degree bank). The earlier RIDE extra yaw (word 00340DDC) did not show in states 1-7, so it is probably not reached; it is left as it was. Vanilla: 3C014220 / 3C0141B0.
patch=1,EE,001C471C,word,3C0141D5
patch=1,EE,001C47F8,word,3C01416A

[Render distance and fog]
author=Shade
description=Farther view distance, terrain and fog on aerial stages.
// 8 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Fog: distance fog (main fog setup): aerial stages 8000-12288, ground stages vanilla =====
// 2026-10-30: FOGC (now at 005BDA00) checks the aerial marker 00340DFC: in aerial stages it forces f12 / f13 = 8000 / 12288 exactly as before; on the ground it multiplies the stage's own fog start and end by 1.0 (2026-10-30: ground stages are vanilla again; was 1.5, 2, 3) before the sub.s.
// The fog setup FUN_0029F36C (called from the frame render function at 00210CDC with f12 = fog start from 00457FB0 and f13 = fog end from 00457FB4) turns the two distances into the slope A = -255 / (end - start) and offset B = 255 * end / (end - start) at 004F4E50 / 004F4E54 and sends them to VU1. Patching the numbers in memory did nothing (the game rewrites them before the call: a state with 30000 / 32000 in memory still had B = 1020 = 255 * 8000 / 2000), so the word at 0029F380 (sub.s f2,f13,f12) becomes j FOGC (005B6800); FOGC loads f12 = 8000.0 (0x45FA0000) and f13 = 12288.0 (0x46400000), redoes the sub.s and jumps back to 0029F388 (the ld in the delay slot still runs). Fog starts at 8000 and is complete at 12288, the end of the view distance (about where the map edge is in your slot-1 view). Applies to every call of the fog setup, i.e. all stages.
patch=1,EE,0029F380,word,0816F680
patch=1,EE,005BDA00,word,3C0B0034
patch=1,EE,005BDA04,word,8D6B0DFC
patch=1,EE,005BDA08,word,11600007
