// ===== Fog: second distance fade (accessors): aerial stages 8000-12288, ground stages vanilla =====
// 2026-10-30: the accessor caves (now at 005BDB00 / 005BDB80) check the aerial marker 00340DFC: aerial stages get near / far 8000 / 12288 as before; ground stages get the stage's own values times 1.0 (vanilla) (f4 is the scratch register).
// A read breakpoint on 00480DC0 stopped in two tiny accessors that read near / far from a0+0x2C0 / a0+0x2C4 (a0 = 00480B00, so 00480DC0 = 5000.0 and 00480DC4 = 8000.0): the one at 002644C0 returns A2 = -128 / (far - near) and the one at 002644F8 returns B2 = far * 128 / (far - near) (341.33 with 5000 / 8000), called from 00252124. This is a second distance fade (scale 128 instead of 255) on top of the one the first fog test removed. The lwc1 at 002644C0 / 002644F8 become j to caves (005B6840 / 005B6860) that load near = 8000.0 and far = 12288.0 into the same registers (the delay-slot lwc1 still runs), then return to 002644C8 / 00264500, so the 128-scale fade runs from 8000 to 12288. The memory patches of the previous test (the 5000 / 8000 pairs) are removed because the game rewrites them.
patch=1,EE,002644C0,word,0816F6C0
