// ===== Render distance: view frustum 1.5625x deeper (about 12500) =====
// Raising the far value at 003AD6FC did nothing (state 2: far 30000 but the frustum corner points at 003AD690..003AD6C0 were still ~12900 from the eye = depth 8000 at the aerial FOV). The culling frustum is built by FUN_002758FC from 5 points (apex + 4 far-plane corners, 16 bytes each, pointer in a1), called from the terrain block builder (00229C50) and from 00129F08 (objects); the planes are made from those points. The word at 00275904 (daddu s0,a1,zero) becomes j FRUS (005B6900); the sd in its delay slot still runs. FRUS copies the 5 points to a scratch buffer at 005B6A00, moving each corner away from the apex by 1.5625 (lui at,0x3FC8 = 1.5625; 0x4014 = 2.3125; 0x4000 = 2.0; 0x4020 = 2.5, 0x4040 = 3, 0x4080 = 4; more than about 2.2 can overflow the 1024-block list of the terrain builder), points a1 at the scratch copy, does the replaced daddu s0,a1,zero and returns to 0027590C. Only culling changes, the projection is untouched, so the terrain and objects are drawn out to 2.5 x the old distance (about 20000). The far-plane test section is removed. 2026-11-06: the hook now goes to FRUSO (005B6B00): when the caller is the object culling (ra = 00129F10, the jal at 00129F08) the frustum is NOT widened (the replaced daddu s0,a1,zero and back to 0027590C), so enemies and other objects are culled at the vanilla distance; the terrain builder (and the third caller at 002647D0) still gets the 1.5625x frustum. Reason: the far depth range (24000) leaves far fewer depth steps beyond the old 8000 limit, and enemies drawn out to 12500 had their own polygons fighting for depth (garbled textures). Not tested in-game.
patch=1,EE,005B6900,word,3C013FC8
patch=1,EE,005B6904,word,44816000
