// ===== Render distance: terrain vertex clip without the far plane (near and side clip kept) =====
// The terrain VU1 microprogram (EE memory 0033F240; 8 bytes per instruction, lower word first) clips each vertex with clipw.xyz vf13,vf13w (upper word 01CD69FF at 0033F56C) and gives flagged vertices the no-draw bit through fcand vi1,0x3FFFF (lower word 2403FFFF at 0033F588). Removing the clipw (previous version) showed the land out to the map edge but made vertices behind the camera or across the near plane produce huge stretched triangles (slots 1 and 2: a tan strip on the left of the screen and flat grey shapes when Angelus flies low). The clipw is restored (the word at 0033F56C is no longer patched) and the fcand mask becomes 0x2FBEF (0x3FFFF without the +z bits 4, 10 and 16: +z means z'' > w'', the far side), so far vertices are no longer discarded while the -z (behind the near plane) and the x / y flags still are: word 2402FBEF at 0033F588.
patch=1,EE,0033F588,word,2402FBEF
// ===== Render distance: terrain block radius 32 on aerial stages, 14 (vanilla) on ground stages =====
// Terrain builder FUN_00229BEC walks a square window of 640-unit blocks around the camera: idx + 64 - R .. idx + 64 + R (64 = the 40960 map offset), R = 14 originally (+-8960 units), now R = 32 (+-20480) so the window covers the 2.3 x deeper frustum (about 18500 deep, 20000 across). The visible blocks go into a list of at most 0x400 entries of 0x1C bytes (stack reserve in 0022A4D0; the loop stops safely when it is full and drops the last rows): about 650 blocks at frustum 2.0, about 870 at 2.3. Words: -0xE / 0x4E / 0x32 at 00229CC8 / 00229CCC / 00229CD0 (x) and 00229CF0 / 00229CF4 / 00229D08 (z) become -0x20 / 0x60 / 0x20. Tune: R = 26 -> -0x1A / 0x5A / 0x26. 2026-11-06: ground stages (aerial marker 00340DFC == 0) use R = 14 (vanilla), aerial stages R = 32. Hook 00229CC0 (lui at,43A0) -> TRC (005B6E00): redoes the lui, sets t7 = -R, t8 = 64 + R, t9 = 64 - R (the third constant was 50 = 64 - 14 originally; 2026-11-06 fix: it had been set to 36 + R = 68 on aerial stages, which gave an empty terrain window); the six addiu of the window (00229CC8 / CCC / CD0 x, 00229CF0 / CF4 / D08 z) are addu with t7 / t8 / t9 (live only in that straight run). Only the block window changes here; the frustum, vertex clip, depth range and edge clamp sections are unchanged for all stages.
patch=1,EE,005B6E00,word,3C0143A0
patch=1,EE,005B6E04,word,3C080034
