patch=1,EE,00229D08,word,00791821
// ===== Render distance: depth range 24000 for all geometry (projection copies) =====
// The combined view-projection matrix (003AD600..003AD630) is built every frame by the matrix multiply FUN_002FC0CC (out = a0, projection A = a1, view B = a2; a write breakpoint on 003AD638 stopped in its store loop, a1 = 003AD580) AFTER the projection rows are rebuilt with O = -64.595 / S = 524756.75, so patching those numbers in memory once per frame never reached it (state 5: patched 003AD5A8 / 003AD5B8 and the copies but the product still had the original depth mapping, and the terrain, now on the original scale, drew its far peaks with negative depth in front of everything). The word at 002FC0EC (lqc2 vf04,0(s1), the first load of A) becomes j MULP (005B6C00); the lqc2 vf05 in its delay slot still runs. MULP, only when s1 = 003AD580 (the projection), writes O = -20.85 (0xC1A6CD61) to s1+0x28 and S = 524406.8 (0x4900076D) to s1+0x38 before the remaining rows (vf06 / vf07) are loaded, redoes lqc2 vf04 and returns to 002FC0F4. z = S / w + O with z = 65530 at w = 8 and z = 1 at w = 24000 (S = 65529 * n * F / (F - n), O = 1 - S / F), so every consumer of the combined matrix (terrain packets, models, enemies, Angelus) shares the same far-24000 depth mapping. Replaces the earlier writes to 003AD5A8 / 003AD5B8 / 005D9F28 / 005D9F38 / 006578C8 / 006578D8.
patch=1,EE,005B6C00,word,3C08003B
patch=1,EE,005B6C04,word,2508D580
patch=1,EE,005B6C08,word,16280007
patch=1,EE,005B6C0C,word,00000000
