patch=1,EE,002FC0EC,word,0816DB00
// ===== Render distance: no terrain outside the map (red band) =====
// Beyond the map edge (blocks outside 0..127) the terrain builder clamps the block index to the edge row/column (0022 9D68 .. 229D94: negative -> 0, > 0x7F -> 0x7F) so the edge data repeats as stretched ridges (the red band in the slot-1 screenshot, about 12800 units from the camera with the map edge at x = -40960). The word at 00229D68 (slti v0,s3,0) becomes j SKIPMAP (005B6C80); the clear a0 in its delay slot still runs. SKIPMAP skips the block (jumps to the loop continue at 00229F04) when the z block s3 or the x block s0 is not in 0..127 (sltiu 0x80), otherwise does the replaced slti and returns to 00229D70. Together with the 12288 view distance and fog the land ends at the map edge in fog.
patch=1,EE,005B6C80,word,2E680080
