// ===== No yellow sky gradient =====
// FUN_002684C4 draws the 10x4 grid of alpha-blended gradient quads (via FUN_00268754) that makes the yellow glow at the top of the screen (found with a GS frame dump). It has no direct callers (virtual call), so it is disabled by returning immediately.
patch=1,EE,002684C4,word,03E00008
patch=1,EE,002684C8,word,00000000
// ===== Menus: 4x faster screen fades (every fade in the game) =====
// Every screen fade goes through the fade manager CFadeMan (task at 004861A8): FadeIn FUN_002761F0 / FadeOut FUN_00276244 (kind, frames; menus pass 0x3C = 60 frames) set a TFader<int> at +0x124, and CFadeMan::Execute (00276CA4) advances it once per frame with TFader<int>::update FUN_0033D6B8 (fader, step), which moves the value by (target - now) / frames left * step. That is its only caller. The jal at 00276CAC now goes to FADE4 (005B7600: sll a1,a1,2 ; j 0033D6B8), so the step is 4 and every fade takes a quarter of the time (60 frames -> 15). Change the 00052880 word (sll a1,a1,2) to 00052840 for 2x or 000528C0 for 8x.
patch=1,EE,005B7600,word,00052880
patch=1,EE,005B7604,word,080CF5AE
patch=1,EE,005B7608,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00276CAC,word,0C16DD80
// ===== Menus: title menu animations 4x =====
// Title menu logic FUN_002DD448 (title menu object 00500648, called every frame by CTitleTask) animates with fixed per-frame steps. After START the menu slides in (states 4 / 5): position 64 -> 19.2 by 2.24 per frame, then -> 0 by 0.96, width 0 -> 64 by 3.2, scale +0.03, three alphas -2 per frame (about 45 frames in all). Going back (states 0xF / 0x10) uses 3.2 / 0.12 / 0.96 / 0.12 / 2.24 and alphas +2; the yes / no popup fades by 4 per frame (states 7 / 9, 0 -> 0x80). All steps are now 4 times larger: the float constants at 00569F80..00569FAC (gp-relative, each used only by this function; the two 19.2 thresholds at 00569F88 / 00569FA4 are unchanged) and the immediates of the addiu instructions at 002DD670 / 68C / 6A4 / 740 / 758 / 770 (-2 -> -8), 002DDC50 / C74 / C98 (+2 -> +8), 002DD9A4 (+4 -> +16) and 002DDA88 (-4 -> -16). Every value has a clamp, so the larger steps cannot overshoot. The menu fade itself (60 frames) is shortened by the fade section.
patch=1,EE,00569F80,word,3DF5C28F
