// ===== Menus: memory card window 4x (load / save popups) =====
// Set to 2x on 2026-10-25 at the user's request: opening step 2 (24620002), closing step -4 (2442FFFC): 32 frames to open, 16 to close.
// The memory card task CMcTask (00508180, Execute FUN_002EA568) animates its popup window ("Load game data?", save / load messages) with the counter +0x134: opening adds 1 per frame up to 0x41 and the task waits until it reaches 0x40 before it goes on (64 frames, over a second, before the window answers); closing subtracts 2 per frame down to 0 (32 frames). The opening step (addiu v0,v1,1 at 002EA94C) is now 4 and the closing step (addiu v0,v0,-2 at 002EA96C) is now -8: 16 frames to open, 8 to close. Both keep their original clamps. The memory card reads and writes themselves are not touched.
patch=1,EE,002EA94C,word,24620002
patch=1,EE,002EA96C,word,2442FFFC
// ===== HUD: widescreen 16:9 (HUD layer only, ground and aerial) =====
// 2026-10-26: aerial reticle now 5/8 size (was 1/2) about its dot centre; marked-enemy rings in layer 0x99 (square REGLIST quads >= 16 px that are not part of the reticle) are halved about their own centre, also when no reticle is found. Stack / scratch moved to 005BA800 / 005BA840 (cave now ends 005BA128).
// 2026-10-30 d: enemy health bars start OFF in every stage: 30 level frames after a stage starts the HUD cave clears 003AB2B0 (object 003AB230 +0x80, the bar toggle the D-left action flips at 001402C4) and calls 0013B258, which copies it to 003A60E4 / 0056A240 (S_BAR counts the frames, reset outside levels; v0 saved around the call). D-left still toggles afterwards. // 2026-10-30 c: the red-screen rule is now screen-wide: pass 14 (before the HUD walk) sets S_RED when any glyph packet of the layer is pure red (RGBAQ R >= 0xE0, G = B = 0); with it set nothing on the layer is shifted left / right. The Game Over Yes / No choice has a dim copy and a highlighted copy; the position rules moved the dim copy 80 px left and (after the per-packet red rule) not the bright one, so the two ended up apart. // 2026-10-30 b: (1) the menu cave only unhooks the dot packet from the chain end tag (base + 0xA30) when the tag points at the dot packet (005A0000 / 005A0600); it had cut off the main text line of the memory card dialog, which is hung on the same tag. (2) pure red glyphs (RGBAQ R >= 0xE0, G = B = 0: the Game Over and Hint screens, which run with every mode task active, so the HUD rules apply) are no longer shifted left / right: the position rules split such a line in two and left a gap in its middle (Red ene   my units). // 2026-10-30: leaving a stage with the lock-on on left the dot on the screen (menus, title, results): outside a level this cave now sets the chain end tag (base + 0xA30) back to END and clears the lock-on bit (00321E2C bit 0), so the dot cave DOT stops drawing. // 2026-10-28 n: cutscene subtitle glitch: the subtitle text sits in the bottom band (centre y 300..360) and was split at x 260 - glyphs left of it were moved left with the portrait (chain-label rule: centre x < 260, y >= 300), glyphs right of it were not moved (or, from x 500, moved right as kill-counter pieces), leaving a gap in the middle of the line. The chain-label rule now covers centre x up to 620 and the kill-counter rule needs centre y >= 380, so the whole line moves left as one block. Gameplay states: no vertex changes. // 2026-10-28 m: the title menu is only vanilla while its selection indicator line is VISIBLE (first colour item alpha >= 0x10 and the line reaches x 630); the game keeps a hidden (alpha 0) copy when you return to the title screen, which made the title screen full size again. Full-width bands (pass 8 y-only path) that reach the top or bottom screen edge keep that edge (y >= 470 -> 480, y <= 10 -> 0), e.g. the chapter select text flap now reaches the bottom of the screen. // 2026-10-28 l: world map: the location label, its text, the selection ring and the map are vanilla (1.0); only the prompts in the top right (layer 0xA1) are scaled to 0.75. // 2026-10-28 k: the options sheet (title task, >= 560 x 250 px, rows baked into its texture) is scaled plainly - the right-edge stretch is only for the chapter page sheets, it had shifted the baked rows away from the text and the music meter; world map: the selection ring (layer 0x9F, 20..50 px square) is scaled to 0.75 about its own centre (pass 12). // 2026-10-28 j: the title menu (NEW GAME / LOAD GAME / OPTIONS; found by its selection indicator line in the pre-pass, S_IND) is left completely vanilla; layer 0xA1 prompt group now = packets in the top / bottom row (centre y >= 440 or <= 48) right of x 100, so the red d-pad icon moves and scales with the Confirm / Return row on every screen; the world map location label is scaled about its bottom-right corner (flush with the screen edges); the options illustration (80 x 256 px, title task) stays 1.0. // 2026-10-28 i: per-screen menu rules (0.75 scale, pass 8 / 9 / 10 / 11): screen flags set before the walks (title task 003B9770 == 0; chapter-map task 003B98B0 == 0 with a pre-pass over layer 0x9A: two full-screen sprites = world map, a 600 x 150 px panel = mode select). Full-screen sprites and the 152 x 134 px portrait ornament stay 1.0; mode select scales only its text glyphs (dark panels 1.0); title menu: the 250..280 x 34..46 px selection indicator line stays 1.0; page sheets (>= 560 x 250 px) are scaled but their right edge is stretched to the screen edge; full-width bands (dialog boxes) keep their full width and are scaled in y; layer 0xA1: wide popup bands 1.0, prompts in the right top / bottom corner scaled about the corner, dialog text about the screen centre (so it stays centred). The world map no longer depends on 00342F6C. The main line of a dialog (e.g. Load game data?) is not in the 2D chain and cannot be moved. // 2026-10-28 h: MENUS now 0.75 (was 0.5): every menu packet except a full-screen one is scaled about the screen centre by the same transform (bands, panels, text and prompts stay aligned; pass 8); prompts layer 0xA1 about the right and bottom/top edge (pass 9); WORLD MAP (chapter-map task 003B98B0 = 0 and 00342F6C != 0): only the location label (box 170..250 x 150..250 px and the glyph sprites after it, about the box centre; pass 10) and the prompts are scaled, the map stays as drawn. // 2026-10-28 g (old 0.5 rules, replaced): MENUS at half size. Outside levels (title, options, memory card windows, button prompts) the cave walks layers 0x9A..0xA3: every packet under 600 px wide is halved about the screen centre (x 0x8000, y 0x7F00); a full-width band under 400 px tall keeps its width and is halved in y only; full-screen backgrounds and fades are left alone; the button prompt layer 0xA1 is halved about the right screen edge and the bottom (or top) edge so the prompts stay in their corner (passes 8 and 9). // 2026-10-28 f: cave MOVED to 005A1000 (it outgrew 005B8300..005BA9xx; the hook 00127334 jumps there; scratch stays at 005BAA00 / 005BAA40). Enemy gauge bars halve about their own centres (only a bar centred inside the frame, and the icon, use the frame centre) so they stay over their heads. While the weapon wheel shows, all of layer 0x99 (the wheel) is halved about the centre of its bounding box (the wheel turns about its hub): passes 6 (box) and 7 (halve). // 2026-10-28 e: fixed-camera (isometric) stages (Caim +0x6B4 = 4): camera object 003ADAC0 holds a stale view there, so the stick rotation (0016ECA0 chain) and the lock-on dot projection were wrong. Each frame the live camera rows 003AD540..0x8F are copied into 003ADB10..; the lock-on camera rule effects (orbit yaw 0013E538, pitch offset 003ADC40) are restored from the previous frame (no camera work). Stack / scratch now 005BAA00 / 005BAA40. // 2026-10-28 d: the wheel is drawn in layers 0x99 / 0x96, not 0x9A; while it shows (stamp or fade words) only the layer 0x99 reticle / ring pass is skipped and the HUD squeeze keeps running (skipping everything made the HUD change size). // 2026-10-28 c: weapon wheel skip = the stamp counter OR the wheel fade words 004F6684 / 004F6688 (non-zero from opening until the closing animation has ended; the input hook runs again during that fade). New pass 4 rules (layer 0x8F): enemy gauges at half size about the frame centre (frame 11 px high and 49 or 65 px wide, 16 px icon, bars 5..9 px high and 20..80 px wide; a lone bar about its own centre). New pass 5 (layer 0x95): kill experience popup text (19 px glyph sprites, shadow first; glyphs of one popup follow each other within 32 x 24 px) at half size about its first glyph. Stack / scratch moved to 005BA900 / 005BA940 (cave ends 005A6554).
// 2026-10-30 e: hint text: in a level, while the stage message buffer still holds the first hint (halfword at 0076F9B6 = Pr and at 0076F9C0 = R3) the cave copies 110 bytes from 005BDF00 over it (section Hint text). The earlier version patched 0076F9B6 every frame and stalled the loading screen. // 2026-10-30 d: enemy health bars start OFF in every stage: 30 level frames after a stage starts the HUD cave clears 003AB2B0 (object 003AB230 +0x80, the bar toggle the D-left action flips at 001402C4) and calls 0013B258, which copies it to 003A60E4 / 0056A240 (S_BAR counts the frames, reset outside levels; v0 saved around the call). D-left still toggles afterwards. // 2026-10-30 c: the red-screen rule is now screen-wide: pass 14 (before the HUD walk) sets S_RED when any glyph packet of the layer is pure red (RGBAQ R >= 0xE0, G = B = 0); with it set nothing on the layer is shifted left / right. The Game Over Yes / No choice has a dim copy and a highlighted copy; the position rules moved the dim copy 80 px left and (after the per-packet red rule) not the bright one, so the two ended up apart. // 2026-10-30 b: (1) the menu cave only unhooks the dot packet from the chain end tag (base + 0xA30) when the tag points at the dot packet (005A0000 / 005A0600); it had cut off the main text line of the memory card dialog, which is hung on the same tag. (2) pure red glyphs (RGBAQ R >= 0xE0, G = B = 0: the Game Over and Hint screens, which run with every mode task active, so the HUD rules apply) are no longer shifted left / right: the position rules split such a line in two and left a gap in its middle (Red ene   my units). // 2026-10-30: leaving a stage with the lock-on on left the dot on the screen (menus, title, results): outside a level this cave now sets the chain end tag (base + 0xA30) back to END and clears the lock-on bit (00321E2C bit 0), so the dot cave DOT stops drawing. // 2026-10-28 n: cutscene subtitle glitch: the subtitle text sits in the bottom band (centre y 300..360) and was split at x 260 - glyphs left of it were moved left with the portrait (chain-label rule: centre x < 260, y >= 300), glyphs right of it were not moved (or, from x 500, moved right as kill-counter pieces), leaving a gap in the middle of the line. The chain-label rule now covers centre x up to 620 and the kill-counter rule needs centre y >= 380, so the whole line moves left as one block. Gameplay states: no vertex changes. // 2026-10-28 m: the title menu is only vanilla while its selection indicator line is VISIBLE (first colour item alpha >= 0x10 and the line reaches x 630); the game keeps a hidden (alpha 0) copy when you return to the title screen, which made the title screen full size again. Full-width bands (pass 8 y-only path) that reach the top or bottom screen edge keep that edge (y >= 470 -> 480, y <= 10 -> 0), e.g. the chapter select text flap now reaches the bottom of the screen. // 2026-10-28 l: world map: the location label, its text, the selection ring and the map are vanilla (1.0); only the prompts in the top right (layer 0xA1) are scaled to 0.75. // 2026-10-28 k: the options sheet (title task, >= 560 x 250 px, rows baked into its texture) is scaled plainly - the right-edge stretch is only for the chapter page sheets, it had shifted the baked rows away from the text and the music meter; world map: the selection ring (layer 0x9F, 20..50 px square) is scaled to 0.75 about its own centre (pass 12). // 2026-10-28 j: the title menu (NEW GAME / LOAD GAME / OPTIONS; found by its selection indicator line in the pre-pass, S_IND) is left completely vanilla; layer 0xA1 prompt group now = packets in the top / bottom row (centre y >= 440 or <= 48) right of x 100, so the red d-pad icon moves and scales with the Confirm / Return row on every screen; the world map location label is scaled about its bottom-right corner (flush with the screen edges); the options illustration (80 x 256 px, title task) stays 1.0. // 2026-10-28 i: per-screen menu rules (0.75 scale, pass 