// 2026-10-30 b: (1) the menu cave only unhooks the dot packet from the chain end tag (base + 0xA30) when the tag points at the dot packet (005A0000 / 005A0600); it had cut off the main text line of the memory card dialog, which is hung on the same tag. (2) pure red glyphs (RGBAQ R >= 0xE0, G = B = 0: the Game Over and Hint screens, which run with every mode task active, so the HUD rules apply) are no longer shifted left / right: the position rules split such a line in two and left a gap in its middle (Red ene   my units). // 2026-10-30: leaving a stage with the lock-on on left the dot on the screen (menus, title, results): outside a level this cave now sets the chain end tag (base + 0xA30) back to END and clears the lock-on bit (00321E2C bit 0), so the dot cave DOT stops drawing. // 2026-10-28 n: cutscene subtitle glitch: the subtitle text sits in the bottom band (centre y 300..360) and was split at x 260 - glyphs left of it were moved left with the portrait (chain-label rule: centre x < 260, y >= 300), glyphs right of it were not moved (or, from x 500, moved right as kill-counter pieces), leaving a gap in the middle of the line. The chain-label rule now covers centre x up to 620 and the kill-counter rule needs centre y >= 380, so the whole line moves left as one block. Gameplay states: no vertex changes. // 2026-10-28 m: the title menu is only vanilla while its selection indicator line is VISIBLE (first colour item alpha >= 0x10 and the line reaches x 630); the game keeps a hidden (alpha 0) copy when you return to the title screen, which made the title screen full size again. Full-width bands (pass 8 y-only path) that reach the top or bottom screen edge keep that edge (y >= 470 -> 480, y <= 10 -> 0), e.g. the chapter select text flap now reaches the bottom of the screen. // 2026-10-28 l: world map: the location label, its text, the selection ring and the map are vanilla (1.0); only the prompts in the top right (layer 0xA1) are scaled to 0.75. // 2026-10-28 k: the options sheet (title task, >= 560 x 250 px, rows baked into its texture) is scaled plainly - the right-edge stretch is only for the chapter page sheets, it had shifted the baked rows away from the text and the music meter; world map: the selection ring (layer 0x9F, 20..50 px square) is scaled to 0.75 about its own centre (pass 12). // 2026-10-28 j: the title menu (NEW GAME / LOAD GAME / OPTIONS; found by its selection indicator line in the pre-pass, S_IND) is left completely vanilla; layer 0xA1 prompt group now = packets in the top / bottom row (centre y >= 440 or <= 48) right of x 100, so the red d-pad icon moves and scales with the Confirm / Return row on every screen; the world map location label is scaled about its bottom-right corner (flush with the screen edges); the options illustration (80 x 256 px, title task) stays 1.0. // 2026-10-28 i: per-screen menu rules (0.75 scale, pass 8 / 9 / 10 / 11): screen flags set before the walks (title task 003B9770 == 0; chapter-map task 003B98B0 == 0 with a pre-pass over layer 0x9A: two full-screen sprites = world map, a 600 x 150 px panel = mode select). Full-screen sprites and the 152 x 134 px portrait ornament stay 1.0; mode select scales only its text glyphs (dark panels 1.0); title menu: the 250..280 x 34..46 px selection indicator line stays 1.0; page sheets (>= 560 x 250 px) are scaled but their right edge is stretched to the screen edge; full-width bands (dialog boxes) keep their full width and are scaled in y; layer 0xA1: wide popup bands 1.0, prompts in the right top / bottom corner scaled about the corner, dialog text about the screen centre (so it stays centred). The world map no longer depends on 00342F6C. The main line of a dialog (e.g. Load game data?) is not in the 2D chain and cannot be moved. // 2026-10-28 h: MENUS now 0.75 (was 0.5): every menu packet except a full-screen one is scaled about the screen centre by the same transform (bands, panels, text and prompts stay aligned; pass 8); prompts layer 0xA1