US now 0.75 (was 0.5): every menu packet except a full-screen one is scaled about the screen centre by the same transform (bands, panels, text and prompts stay aligned; pass 8); prompts layer 0xA1 about the right and bottom/top edge (pass 9); WORLD MAP (chapter-map task 003B98B0 = 0 and 00342F6C != 0): only the location label (box 170..250 x 150..250 px and the glyph sprites after it, about the box centre; pass 10) and the prompts are scaled, the map stays as drawn. // 2026-10-28 g (old 0.5 rules, replaced): MENUS at half size. Outside levels (title, options, memory card windows, button prompts) the cave walks layers 0x9A..0xA3: every packet under 600 px wide is halved about the screen centre (x 0x8000, y 0x7F00); a full-width band under 400 px tall keeps its width and is halved in y only; full-screen backgrounds and fades are left alone; the button prompt layer 0xA1 is halved about the right screen edge and the bottom (or top) edge so the prompts stay in their corner (passes 8 and 9). // 2026-10-28 f: cave MOVED to 005A1000 (it outgrew 005B8300..005BA9xx; the hook 00127334 jumps there; scratch stays at 005BAA00 / 005BAA40). Enemy gauge bars halve about their own centres (only a bar centred inside the frame, and the icon, use the frame centre) so they stay over their heads. While the weapon wheel shows, all of layer 0x99 (the wheel) is halved about the centre of its bounding box (the wheel turns about its hub): passes 6 (box) and 7 (halve). // 2026-10-28 e: fixed-camera (isometric) stages (Caim +0x6B4 = 4): camera object 003ADAC0 holds a stale view there, so the stick rotation (0016ECA0 chain) and the lock-on dot projection were wrong. Each frame the live camera rows 003AD540..0x8F are copied into 003ADB10..; the lock-on camera rule effects (orbit yaw 0013E538, pitch offset 003ADC40) are restored from the previous frame (no camera work). Stack / scratch now 005BAA00 / 005BAA40. // 2026-10-28 d: the wheel is drawn in layers 0x99 / 0x96, not 0x9A; while it shows (stam