// 2026-10-28 c: weapon wheel skip = the stamp counter OR the wheel fade words 004F6684 / 004F6688 (non-zero from opening until the closing animation has ended; the input hook runs again during that fade). New pass 4 rules (layer 0x8F): enemy gauges at half size about the frame centre (frame 11 px high and 49 or 65 px wide, 16 px icon, bars 5..9 px high and 20..80 px wide; a lone bar about its own centre). New pass 5 (layer 0x95): kill experience popup text (19 px glyph sprites, shadow first; glyphs of one popup follow each other within 32 x 24 px) at half size about its first glyph. Stack / scratch moved to 005BA900 / 005BA940 (cave ends 005BA850).
// 2026-10-28 b: the weapon wheel skip no longer uses a game flag (both tried ones depended on the wheel data layout). The player input hook 0013E528 (Aerial core section) clears 005BBFF0 every gameplay frame and does not run while the wheel is open; the HUD cave counts it up and skips while it is 3 or more.
// 2026-10-28: the weapon wheel skip now tests 004F6684 (wheel opacity, 128 open / 0 closed); 004F6624 stayed 1 after the wheel had been used once, which switched the whole HUD cave off in normal play. New pass 4: the yellow TARGET marker (layer 0x8F, one 64 x 42 px sprite) is drawn at half size about its centre.
// 2026-10-27: also skipped while the weapon wheel is open (004F6624 != 0), like the pause map; the squeeze rules tore the wheel pieces apart.
// Clean widescreen HUD. The 2D library builds each frame into one DMA chain buffer (base word 004F50D0; 0xA4 layer heads of 16 bytes, each a NEXT tag to that layer's packets; every 2D drawing function writes to a fixed layer through its tail pointer 004F50D8 + 4 * layer). Save states of ground, riding and aerial play show that the screen-fixed HUD (gauge, kill count, compass and its blips, mission dialogue box) is in layer 0x9A, while the aerial reticle and dots are in layer 0x99, the lock-on dot / ride reticle are appended at the end of the chain, and 3D and effects are in other layers. The jr ra that ends the chain builder FUN_001270E8 (00127334; its delay slot addiu sp,sp,0x20 still runs, and the lock-on dot cave returns through it too) becomes j HUDX (005B8300). HUDX runs only in levels (the title, chapter map, result, title call and weapon select tasks all inactive, and not while the pause map / menu is open: word 003ADC50 = 1) and walks only layer 0x9A of the frame just built (cnt / next / call / ret / ref tags; it follows a call or ref only when the target is inside this frame's buffer, so shared static packets and textures are never touched; image uploads are skipped; at most 3000 tags), once, and moves the vertices of every REGLIST or PACKED packet (XYZ2 / XYZF2 / XYZ3 / XYZF3, or A+D to XYZ): x is squeezed by 3/4 about the screen centre (x16 = ((x16 - 0x8000) * 3 >> 2) + 0x8000) and the packet is then moved 80 px (0x500) toward its corner, chosen from its original bounding box: kill counter and its effects (angel icon and expanding rings; anything centred right of x 500 and below y 300) and compass with its blips (inside x 480..640, y 20..145, the rim blips included, and at most 16 px or at least 60 px tall: dialogue glyphs are 24 px tall and are drawn first in the layer, so a long dialogue line reaching into the compass box stays in one piece) go right as long as no dialogue-box piece (outside the compass box, starting above y 60, 250 px wide or more) came earlier in the layer that frame: the compass is always drawn before the dialogue box, so it stays right while it fades out and the dialogue text that follows the box goes left in one piece; the dialogue box (anything starting above y 230), the gauge (anything starting below y 360: frame, emblem, bar and bead rows, which are dozens of 16 px pieces reaching x 486) its tall left ornament (max x <= 120) and the chain counter label and gauge effects (anything centred left of x 260 and below y 300, e.g. the CHAIN text beside the chain numbers) go left; anything else stays. Packets 600 px wide or wider (full-screen overlays) are left alone. Registers: only at, v1, a0-a3, t0-t9 (v0 kept; no stack); stack and scratch at 005BA000..005BA0C3. PAUSE CAMERA: the pause map turns the player camera straight down (angle words 003ADC40 / 003ADC44; pitch becomes -pi/2) and the game never turns it back. On every gameplay frame (pause flag 004EE29C = 0) HUDX keeps a copy of both angles; after the flag clears it eases the camera back over 40 frames (each frame angle += (copy - angle) * 0.15, FPU temporaries f4-f6), so the camera turns smoothly back to where it was before the pause. The copy is forgotten outside levels. LOCK-ON CAMERA SMOOTHING RESET: when the lock-on rule did not apply a camera step in a frame (word 005AF1F8 left 0 by FILT: lock off, no target, riding) the smoothed turn speeds 005AF1F0 / 005AF1F4 are zeroed; the word is cleared every frame. KNOCKDOWN 1.5x: while Caim (003AC5E0) is in the damage state (+0x2D0 = 5) after a knockdown clip (+0x120 = 0x48..0x4A; marked until he leaves the state, so the get-up is included) the playback rate of his animation request (+0x174, read every frame) is set to 1.5x the value the game wrote (the written value is kept in scratch so it is not raised again). FASTER RIDDEN TURN: while Angelus is ridden on a ground stage and steered (target lean dragon 0041BFC0 +0xB4 beyond 0.05) the heading (+0xA0, wrapped -pi..pi) gets the change the game made since the last frame added once more, so she turns twice as fast; steps of 0.2 rad or more (U-turn) are left alone. (An earlier section doubled the lean instead; the riding camera is built from her rolled body, so it rolled over and sank below the ground. That section was removed.) DISMOUNT CAMERA: the on-foot camera keeps its own world angles (camera object 003ADAC0 +0x40 pitch / +0x44 yaw = 003ADB00 / 003ADB04), frozen while Caim rides, and switches back to them when he gets off, so the view snapped to the direction he faced when he mounted. While Caim rides (003AC5E0 +0x6B4 = 2) HUDX copies the live angles (003AD530 / 003AD534) into them every frame, and the game's ring of camera records it restores from on the dismount (005B4500, 108 slots of 0x40; valid records have +0x28 = 3 and +0x2C = 8 and exist only while riding; +0x04 / +0x18 yaw, +0x0C offset = yaw - Caim facing (Caim +0x44), wrapped to -pi .. pi) gets the live yaw and that offset too, and on foot the camera looks along Caim's facing (+0x44) + the offset 003ADC44, which the game fills from yet another stale copy of the pre-mount view on the dismount. So for 60 frames after the dismount (Caim +0x6B4 2 -> 1) HUDX owns the yaw: T starts at the last riding yaw and each frame moves 8% of the way (wrapped) toward Caim's facing; the live yaw 003AD534, the saved yaw 003ADB04 and the offset 003ADC44 = T - facing are all written from it, so the camera turns smoothly from the riding view to look where Caim faces. SCRIPT PANELS: the two faint script panels behind the gauge vine (sprites originally 0..104 x 240..480 and 104..200 x 368..490) leave an L-shaped edge, so their RGBAQ alpha is set to 0 (not drawn; the vine in the same texture goes with them, at user request). BRIEFING MAP: a parchment starting above y 10, 280 px or more tall and 200..480 px wide (the mission briefing map) and every later piece inside its box get one shift that centres the map on screen; while it is up, the lock-on dot / star tag at chain base + 0xA30 (the end of the whole chain, which DOT turns into a NEXT to its packet) is set back to an END tag (70000000, 0) and the reticle layer 0x99 head is made an empty layer (NEXT to the 0x9A head), so no reticle is drawn. (Pointing the A30 tag at base + 0xA40 froze the game: nothing valid follows the chain end.) AERIAL RETICLE HALF SIZE: after the HUD walk, layer 0x99 (aerial reticle) is walked twice: first the four orange dots (REGLIST sprites at most 10 x 10 px) are found; if exactly four, spanning under 90 px, every packet whose vertices are ALL within 64 px of their centre (blades and dots; the large enemy target rings in the same layer have far corners and are left alone) is moved halfway to the centre (x = (x + cx) / 2, y likewise; y at +2 in REGLIST, +4 in PACKED). Verified in an emulator model against a Python reference on the save states (0 mismatching bytes; nothing outside layer 0x9A changed; no change on title / chapter map states). The dialogue parchment (starts above y 10, 300 px wide or more, reaching x 630+) keeps its right-edge vertices at their original x, so it still runs off the screen edge instead of ending in a hard seam mid-screen.
// 2026-11-06: the aerial reticle shrink (layers 0x99, passes 2 / 3 of build_hud.py) only found Angelus form 1's reticle (four orange dots) and drew the form 2 reticle (six dots) full size. Pass 2 now also accepts six dots (scratch word S_RM = 0x5BAB58: 0 = four dots, 1 = six) and pass 3 draws the six dot reticle at 15/32 of its size ((15 v + 17 c) / 32 about the dots' centre) instead of 5/8, so its dots end up at the same distance from the centre as form 1's (27 x 15/32 = 12.7 px against 20 x 5/8 = 12.5 px).
// 2026-11-06: dismount camera. DISMOUNT_K is 0: after the landing (+0x6B4 2 -> 1) the 60 frame window keeps the camera yaw at T = the last riding yaw (S_TYAW, updated on every riding frame including the dismount jump) instead of easing it to Caim's facing. A "hold the yaw during the jump" block was tried (write 005A12A4) and removed: it kept S_TYAW at the pre-jump value, so the window (write 005A1474, found with a write breakpoint on 003AD534: the camera snapped exactly at that store) put the camera back to a stale yaw at the landing. The game itself writes the live yaw (0012049C) from the camera matrix every frame. FOUND (the user's states 1 / 2: 1 = last jump frame, live yaw 1.857 = Caim's facing, correct; 2 = landed, live yaw -0.619 = W): the ground free camera (section world-fixed 360 orbit; world yaw W at 0013E538, forces the final yaw to W once Caim is on foot) was the cause. W is only changed by the right stick on foot, so it still held the orbit yaw from before the ride and the camera snapped to it at the landing, whatever the window wrote. Fix: on every riding frame (+0x6B4 = 2) and in the 60 frame window W (0013E538) is set to the live / held yaw, so the free camera takes over exactly where the riding view (Caim's facing at the end of the jump) ended. A version that set Caim's facing to the camera yaw was tried and removed on request (build_hud.py.bak_caimyaw). Camera control (user states, 9 saves after a dismount): the 60 frame window held the live yaw at T for a second after the landing, so the camera resisted the stick (states: DMT 57 -> 7, live yaw fixed at -2.904, then free at DMT 0). With W carrying the direction the window is not needed: DISMOUNT_FRAMES is now 2 (build_hud.py.bak_window60), so the free camera has full control from the third frame after the landing.
// 2026-11-06 c: MENU DIALOG TEXT. The Yes / No question and description line of the dragon / ally selection (layer 0x9B glyphs, at most 40 x 40 px, centre y 355..470) were scaled about the screen centre (0.75) and so ended above the dark bottom box (layer 0xA4, not scaled). In menu pass 8 such packets are now scaled about their own vertical centre (x still about the screen centre), so they stay inside the box. Not tested in-game.
// 2026-11-06 d: AERIAL RETICLE FORM 3. Form 3 draws eight orange dots on a ring of 31 px radius (the same radius as the six dots of form 2; form 1 four dots 23 px); the walk only knew four or six dots, so form 3 stayed full size. Eight dots now use the form 2 rule (15/32, ring radius 14.5 px, the same as forms 1 and 2). Checked in the emulator on two saved form 3 states (31 -> 14.5 and 7 -> 3.3 px). Not tested in-game.
