// ===== Weapon specials: no screen flash =====
// The ground attack state FUN_0017C14C starts the screen effect 4 (type 2 colour flash 80282828 -> 80100808, 1.4 s, drawn by the screen effect manager 0040CD58 into 2D layer 0x97) when a weapon special starts: jal 001A02F4 at 0017C9E8 (a0 = 4). That jal becomes a nop (its delay slot addiu a1,zero,1 is harmless). Other screen effects (fades etc.) are untouched; the special's own glow particles stay.
patch=1,EE,0017C9E8,word,00000000

[Enemies and allies]
author=Shade
description=Enemy squad range, aggro, projectile speeds and ally attack speeds.
// 6 original sections merged here (the comment lines headed by ===== name ===== are the original sections).
// ===== Enemies: squads wake up and stay active from 1.5x farther away =====
// Each enemy squad copies three distance thresholds every frame (FUN_00167F78, called from the squad update) from the table at 003BA2D0 (4 rows x 16 bytes, row picked by the game mode FUN_0017DFF8 == 2 and squad flags +0x9B4 bits 2 / 4) into +0x9B8 / +0x9BC / +0x9C0. +0xE4 is the world distance from Caim to the squad (camera arm = 68 units). FUN_00166FB4 reports the squad out of range when +0xE4 >= +0x9BC and the squad update then removes it (FUN_001669DC); FUN_00167FFC turns the distance into an activity level with all three (the 190 one is where a sleeping squad wakes up). Vanilla rows: 0 = 400 / 320 / 190 (normal), 1 = 650 / 500 / 210, 2 = 800 / 750 / 600, 3 = 10000 / 9900 / 9800 (special squads, left alone). Rows 0..2 are 1.5x here (normal squads: wake at 285, removed at 480; was 2x until 2026-10-30, 3x before 2026-10-28). Found from save states: the vanished squad sat at 320.2 from Caim, then 338.6 when it was gone. To tune, change the factor in these floats (1.5x: 600 / 480 / 285 ...). Watch for slowdown or mission triggers with many squads active.
patch=1,EE,003BA2D0,word,44160000
