// ===== Angelus: Caim is knocked off by chance depending on health while riding (normal damage) =====
// Ridden Angelus: every hit does normal (1x) damage; Caim is knocked off by chance depending on his health after the hit (> 50% of +0x284: never; 26-50%: 25%; 1-25%: 50%). DMG rolls (xorshift word 005BEE04) on every hit and leaves the result in word 005BEE00; CLAMP turns it into s3 = 1 with the gauge set to 0x5001 (like the game's own gauge knock-off). 00179214 (invulnerability 0x800 at zero health) is nopped so Caim stays hittable at 1 HP. Older description: FUN_00179100 (Caim = s1, the rider damage function; Angelus = Caim +0x6B0, its hit flag +0x424 is set by the Angelus hit function 0017E8C8) subtracts the damage s0 (from FUN_00194D80, called at 001791A8) from Caim's health (+0x280) and adds a stability value to the gauge +0x770; it returns 1 (= knocked off) when the health runs out (001791F8..00179204, addiu s3,zero,1) or the gauge goes above 0x5000 (movz s3 at 00179260). - 001791A8 jal 00194D80 -> jal DMG: calls the real function and leaves its result unchanged (ra saved in word 005BEBF4). - 00179204 and 00179260 become nops (s3 stays 0: never knocked off). Health still stops at 1 (the game's own floor), so Caim cannot die while riding. - 00179264 (lw v0,0x770(s1)) -> j CLAMP: the gauge is held at 0x5000 at most (so the flag +0x428 and the gauge test of the mount code stay 'normal'). Not tested in-game.
patch=1,EE,005BEC80,word,3C08005C
patch=1,EE,005BEC84,word,AD1FEE08
patch=1,EE,005BEC88,word,0C065360
