// 2026-11-14 right stick ignored while the pause menu is open (word 004EE29C == 1): the pad reader FUN_001288A8 (a0 = pad copy, a1 = index; returns the byte at +0x14+index) is hooked: 001288A8 = j PADR (5B9600), 001288AC = nop (its sltiu is redone in the cave); in PADR, when the pause flag is set and the index is 0 or 1 (right stick x / y) the reader returns 0x80 (centre) and, on every call while paused, the raw right stick bytes 00342864 / 00342865 are set to 0x80 too (the Angelus caves that test 00342865 directly: reticle / fireball drop 005B8900.., camera look-down 005B8A50, AIM 005B8D00 then see the stick centred), else the original instructions run and it jumps back to 001288B0.
